1
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:41,941
DO YOU HEAR MY APPEAL?

2
00:00:41,965 --> 00:00:46,067
IN MY SEVERE TRIBULATION AND DISRESS

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:54,609
DO YOU HEAR MY GRON, MY AGONY AND MY CRYING?

4
00:00:54,633 --> 00:01:03,051
GLAD TIDING TO MY NATION, THEY RAISED TO THE RANK OF MARTYRS,

5
00:01:03,075 --> 00:01:11,426
MY CONDOLENCES ARE NOT TO THEM, BUT RATER FOR THE MUSLIMS

6
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:19,935
DO YOU HEAR MY GRON, MY AGONY AND MY CRYING?

7
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:23,004
GLAD TIDING TO MY NATION,

8
00:01:23,028 --> 00:01:24,706
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

9
00:01:27,153 --> 00:01:28,642
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

10
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:32,230
 اَلْحَمْدُ لله رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ۝

11
00:01:32,389 --> 00:01:37,530
وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ صَلَوَاتُ الله وَالسَلامُ عَلَيْهَِ

12
00:01:41,657 --> 00:01:45,860
All of you, want to learn, Islamic knowledge.

13
00:01:46,882 --> 00:01:50,298
We have been saying that again and again, everyone says; I want to learn.

14
00:01:52,175 --> 00:01:58,691
Brothers and Sisters alike, are very eager to learn Islam and that’s a very good sign, Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله)

15
00:01:58,797 --> 00:02:06,147
It's one of the things, that is found among the young generation

16
00:02:07,086 --> 00:02:11,200
and this was not something to be found in the generation of their fathers.

17
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:20,084
The zeal and eagerness you have, to learn today is definitely more than, the generation before you.

18
00:02:20,893 --> 00:02:24,366
So, that’s a good sign it’s a sign of the awakening of Ummah(أمة)

19
00:02:25,151 --> 00:02:30,011
and it’s a sign that Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) even though may be,

20
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:37,030
in other areas the situation is getting worse, politically it's getting worse.

21
00:02:39,082 --> 00:02:43,980
However, when you want to assess a situation

22
00:02:44,521 --> 00:02:49,247
don’t look at the political realities or the economical realities, but look at the human factor.

23
00:02:50,998 --> 00:02:57,999
If the people are improving then you will see the improvement in the other areas early on.

24
00:02:58,615 --> 00:03:04,805
It's the human resource that's the most important factor in any change in human history.

25
00:03:05,724 --> 00:03:09,443
And that change Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) is happening among many of the youth.

26
00:03:10,086 --> 00:03:15,399
So, everybody wants to learn, they sign up for a courses, and they go and study, and they travel overseas and...

27
00:03:18,669 --> 00:03:25,915
However, many of you are saying; We are not learning enough, we want to learn more.

28
00:03:26,649 --> 00:03:31,903
Many of you are saying, we are not given Islamic knowledge enough time, right?

29
00:03:32,703 --> 00:03:34,663
You all feel that you want to do more.

30
00:03:36,141 --> 00:03:40,408
And what is holding you back from giving more time to studying Islam?

31
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:46,481
You are busy! You have work to do! You want to make a living!!

32
00:03:47,374 --> 00:03:51,714
And if you are not trying to make living yet because your parents are taking care of your expenses,

33
00:03:52,425 --> 00:03:55,803
you are studying!!! You are going to college, university,

34
00:03:58,197 --> 00:04:02,765
and you are complaining that you don’t have enough time need to study Islamic Shari’ah(شريعة)

35
00:04:04,611 --> 00:04:05,559
Right??

36
00:04:07,217 --> 00:04:14,953
Now, are you assuming that, the Sahabah(صحابه) didn’t have any work to do?

37
00:04:16,619 --> 00:04:19,814
How come, they were able to learn and you aren't able to learn?

38
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:25,524
Well, you might say, Oh, we are living in 21st Century!!!

39
00:04:26,286 --> 00:04:32,427
Things are complicated now, and life had become very difficult and we have to work, more.

40
00:04:34,099 --> 00:04:36,030
If that’s your assumption, you are wrong.

41
00:04:37,401 --> 00:04:39,501
In fact you have more time than the Sahabah(صحابه).

42
00:04:40,291 --> 00:04:50,484
The Sahabah(صحابه) had to make a living none of them was born with a golden or silver spoon in their mouth they had to work.

43
00:04:53,158 --> 00:04:58,820
In fact, their commitment to work was more difficult than yours.

44
00:04:59,366 --> 00:05:03,909
You now, work from 9:00 to 5:00 or from 8:00 to 4:00

45
00:05:03,982 --> 00:05:08,442
Allah Ho Aalam(الله اعلم) what your schedule is, in this country but then you have Saturday and Sunday off.

46
00:05:08,572 --> 00:05:11,380
And after 5:00PM you go back home you are free.

47
00:05:11,845 --> 00:05:13,681
Well Sahabah(صحابه) didn’t work in offices.

48
00:05:13,721 --> 00:05:17,338
The Sahabah(صحابه) were shepherds or they were farmers or they were businessmen.

49
00:05:18,842 --> 00:05:22,380
And as a shepherd you cannot go to your cows and say;

50
00:05:23,603 --> 00:05:25,470
O my cows see you next week,

51
00:05:26,011 --> 00:05:28,783
I am not going to be here Saturday and Sunday, you can’t do that.

52
00:05:30,132 --> 00:05:31,853
You have to feed them every day.

53
00:05:33,003 --> 00:05:36,849
You can’t go to your farm and tell them your plants that I am going to be off for a month.

54
00:05:37,751 --> 00:05:39,186
I am taking a summer vacation.

55
00:05:40,561 --> 00:05:42,992
Your plants if you don’t show up, they are gonna die.

56
00:05:43,531 --> 00:05:45,681
You have to be there for them every day.

57
00:05:48,648 --> 00:05:50,371
And in those days business was tough.

58
00:05:52,633 --> 00:05:55,085
So, you have to put a lot of effort and time in it.

59
00:05:57,037 --> 00:06:00,640
So, how come the Sahaba(صحابه) were able to do both?

60
00:06:01,537 --> 00:06:10,214
How come they were able to study, from Rasool Allah ﷺ and in the same time they were able to make a living?

61
00:06:11,356 --> 00:06:18,266
You know the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, they were very active.

62
00:06:19,659 --> 00:06:26,119
They were furthest from being lazy, they were not living off benefits, we found in the U.S. welfare.

63
00:06:26,833 --> 00:06:30,216
Sahabah رضي الله عنهم they had to go out and make a living for themselves.

64
00:06:30,582 --> 00:06:32,781
Yes some of them were poor like Ahlus Suffah(اهل الصُّفة),

65
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:41,273
and if they had a chance to work they would work because we know that

66
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:47,259
many of these Ahlus Suffah(اهل الصُّفة) they would go out to the area in Madina called Al-Ghaba(ألغابة) the forest,

67
00:06:47,307 --> 00:06:53,397
 and they would go there cut down fire work and come and sell it in Madina.

68
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:56,473
So when there is work, they are gonna work.

69
00:06:56,813 --> 00:06:58,979
But there just wasn’t any work to do.

70
00:06:59,508 --> 00:07:00,983
That’s why they were unemployed.

71
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:10,334
So, how did they do it, how come we are failing today, while they were successful in their endeavors.?

72
00:07:11,528 --> 00:07:12,735
Let's see how Umar(عُمَر) did it?

73
00:07:15,335 --> 00:07:21,790
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه had some business to take care of, he had some also pieces of land.

74
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:29,377
He had a partner from among Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), he made an agreement,

75
00:07:29,552 --> 00:07:32,740
and they used to live on the outskirts of Madina, the suburbs.

76
00:07:33,444 --> 00:07:42,431
He made an agreement, with his Ansaari(أنصاري) companion, partner that

77
00:07:45,296 --> 00:07:55,457
I am gonna work one day and you go down to Madina and accompany Rasool Allah ﷺ for the whole day.

78
00:07:56,309 --> 00:08:02,662
And then when you come back at night, we meet and you report to me, everything Rasool Allah ﷺ said.

79
00:08:04,528 --> 00:08:10,214
And then the next day, I am going to, go down to Madina while you pick up my work.

80
00:08:10,891 --> 00:08:12,017
So, they were alternate.

81
00:08:13,190 --> 00:08:18,238
One day Umar(عُمَر) would work and the Ansaari(أنصاري) is studying and vice versa.

82
00:08:20,761 --> 00:08:30,836
What this meant Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and his partner would end up doing double the effort, double the work.

83
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:34,401
Because Umar(عُمَر) would have to do his work and his partners work,

84
00:08:35,501 --> 00:08:39,459
and his partner would have to do his work and Umar(عُمَر)’s work.

85
00:08:40,616 --> 00:08:41,864
So, this tells you something.

86
00:08:42,372 --> 00:08:48,144
As a Muslim you're gonna have to make a living just like the Kafir(كافر).

87
00:08:48,247 --> 00:08:52,669
You know, Allahعَزّ وجَلّ does not differentiate between Muslim and Kafir(كافر) when it comes to Rizq(رزق).

88
00:08:53,203 --> 00:08:59,941
You all have to go out and work, human beings, animals, plants, you have to make a living.

89
00:09:01,142 --> 00:09:05,199
Even when Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to teach us about Tawakul(توكل) what did Rasool Allah ﷺsay?

90
00:09:06,078 --> 00:09:09,223
لَوْ أَنَّكُمْ تَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ عَلى الله حَقَّ تَوَّكُّلِهْ

91
00:09:09,410 --> 00:09:11,943
لَرُزِقْتُمْ كَمَا تُرْزَقَ الطَّيْرْ،

92
00:09:12,179 --> 00:09:14,661
 تَغْدُوْ خِمَاصًا وَتَرُوْحُ بِطَانًاَ

93
00:09:15,212 --> 00:09:19,855
If you have the right Tawakul(توكل) on Allah,

94
00:09:20,405 --> 00:09:24,052
then Allah will give you Rizq(رزق) like he is giving the birds.

95
00:09:25,508 --> 00:09:29,367
They leave in the morning hungry and they come back at night full.

96
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:34,662
Notice that Hadith did not say that the birds are staying at home, sitting on their nests,

97
00:09:35,271 --> 00:09:37,308
holding a remote control and watching TV.

98
00:09:38,623 --> 00:09:45,490
They went out early in the morning and they came back at night, working for the whole day and that’s Tawakul(توكل).

99
00:09:45,704 --> 00:09:47,802
That Hadith(حديث) is the definition of Tawakul(توكل).

100
00:09:49,013 --> 00:09:56,400
So, the birds had to do a lot of work from morning to sunset, but then, they come back full.

101
00:09:57,963 --> 00:10:00,900
So, when it comes to Rizq(رزق) you have to work like everybody else.

102
00:10:00,948 --> 00:10:03,737
Just because you are a Muslim don’t think that you will be spoon fed.

103
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:09,608
When it comes to Rizq(رزق) in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) everybody has to go out and work for it.

104
00:10:10,417 --> 00:10:12,700
However, there is a difference between you and the Kafir(كافر).

105
00:10:13,252 --> 00:10:15,819
The Kafir(كافر) all what he wants is to make a living in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

106
00:10:16,064 --> 00:10:21,642
but as a Muslim you are making a living in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) in order to take you to the Akhirah(آخرة),

107
00:10:21,666 --> 00:10:24,109
Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) for you is a bridge to Akhirah(آخرة).

108
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:33,894
So, you have an additional effort which is your Akhirah(آخرة) and that means, that in order for you as a Muslim to succeed

109
00:10:34,222 --> 00:10:38,831
you have to do the double the effort of a Kafir(كافر) is doing, double.

110
00:10:39,882 --> 00:10:44,767
You can't be on an equal footing, you have to put in, double the work,

111
00:10:46,096 --> 00:10:48,322
double the time, double the effort.

112
00:10:51,843 --> 00:10:58,388
Because if you don’ t since you are holding the two items in your plate, you'll end up failing in both.

113
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:07,983
So, if the system of Rizq(رزق) today is so complicated that it demands a lot of time from you.

114
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:12,193
The only way for you is to succeed in both Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Akhirah(آخرة)

115
00:11:13,283 --> 00:11:21,010
is for you to cut off time from your entertainment, from your sleep, you have to do, what you have to do.

116
00:11:24,083 --> 00:11:28,728
So as a Muslim you cannot afford to waste single moment of your life,

117
00:11:29,370 --> 00:11:30,650
not a Single Moment.

118
00:11:31,563 --> 00:11:39,309
A Muslim cannot afford to waste any time because the clock for you is ticking and it’s a countdown, for you it's a countdown.

119
00:11:39,802 --> 00:11:43,975
 You see the way the Kuffar(كفار), or some of the Kuffar(كفار) see it,

120
00:11:45,064 --> 00:11:48,822
is that we are in a fight with nature

121
00:11:50,848 --> 00:11:56,560
and every year that passes by, we have won against nature.

122
00:11:56,839 --> 00:12:02,953
At least that was the perception in the old Europe, it’s a fight between us and nature.

123
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:14,037
You know, in some societies they used to view that they are in harmony with the nature

124
00:12:14,084 --> 00:12:20,061
for example with the Native Americans, their world view is that we are in harmony with the nature.

125
00:12:20,356 --> 00:12:24,832
So, they wouldn’t touch the environment, they wouldn't harm it, because they believe that we all are one.

126
00:12:25,544 --> 00:12:32,073
However, in the western mind, it’s a challenge between us and nature, it's a fight,

127
00:12:33,492 --> 00:12:35,535
and that’s why, they celebrate birthdays.

128
00:12:36,199 --> 00:12:38,601
You find that birthdays is a big thing in the west. Why?

129
00:12:39,449 --> 00:12:41,273
Because in the old days when life was rough

130
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:48,610
and you know, you had a few months in the year when you cannot plant, you cannot farm in winter,

131
00:12:49,171 --> 00:12:50,730
so life for them was struggle.

132
00:12:51,791 --> 00:12:58,129
So, when they live for another year, they see that they had won against the forces of nature, so they celebrate birthday.

133
00:12:59,185 --> 00:13:03,427
I have lived for another year and I have defeated the forces of nature

134
00:13:03,461 --> 00:13:05,273
therefore, I should celebrate my birthday.

135
00:13:07,202 --> 00:13:11,112
But that’s not the world view of a Muslim.

136
00:13:11,543 --> 00:13:14,072
A Muslim believes that your life is already destined.

137
00:13:15,048 --> 00:13:18,855
You are not fighting with nature, your life is already destined.

138
00:13:19,202 --> 00:13:24,892
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ has already ordained the exact time you will spend in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

139
00:13:25,884 --> 00:13:30,131
so when a year passes by the way you should see it as a Muslim,

140
00:13:31,028 --> 00:13:34,870
you should see it that I am one year closer to my death.

141
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:38,593
I am getting closer to my grave.

142
00:13:40,023 --> 00:13:43,720
So it doesn’t make any sense whatsoever, for you as a Muslim

143
00:13:44,189 --> 00:13:47,918
to bring a cake in front of you blow the candles and you are smiling and so happy,

144
00:13:48,545 --> 00:13:51,505
when you are one year closer to your death, you should be making Mahasibah(محاسبه).

145
00:13:52,335 --> 00:13:57,275
You should be holding yourself accountable for that year not celebrating and taking photos in front of a cake.

146
00:13:58,897 --> 00:14:01,373
You should be viewing it with seriousness.

147
00:14:01,785 --> 00:14:04,878
I am one year closer in meeting Allahعَزّ وجَلّ .

148
00:14:05,442 --> 00:14:08,506
What have I done, did I have prepare myself for it?

149
00:14:08,914 --> 00:14:09,879
حَاسِبُوْا أَنْفُسَكُمْ

150
00:14:09,903 --> 00:14:11,396
one of the statements of Umar(عُمَر) was:

151
00:14:11,717 --> 00:14:13,815
حَاسِبُوْا أَنْفُسَكُمْ قَبْلَ أَنْ تُحَاسِبُوْا

152
00:14:14,364 --> 00:14:17,954
Hold yourself accountable before you will be hold accountable, for what you did.?

153
00:14:22,521 --> 00:14:27,876
So, if you want to succeed you going to have to find a formula like Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه did.

154
00:14:36,176 --> 00:14:38,629
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) has narrated many Ahadith(احاديث).

155
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:44,824
One of them for example, is considered to be one quarter of Islam according to Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

156
00:14:45,751 --> 00:14:48,932
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) considers, this Hadith(حديث) to be one quarter of Islam.

157
00:14:50,548 --> 00:14:52,115
And which Hadith(حديث) is that?

158
00:14:53,004 --> 00:14:58,123
It’s the first Hadith(حديث) in Al-Arba’on An-Nawwawia(اَلْاَرْبَعُوْنَ النَّوَّوَيَّةْ).

159
00:14:59,347 --> 00:15:00,296
What is the Hadith(حديث)?

160
00:15:02,175 --> 00:15:04,012
إِنَّمَا الْأَعْمَالُ بِالنِّيَّاتِ،

161
00:15:05,233 --> 00:15:07,870
Deeds are in accordance to the intentions.

162
00:15:08,858 --> 00:15:11,406
This Hadith(حديث) was narrated by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

163
00:15:11,431 --> 00:15:14,140
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه has narrated many Ahadith(احاديث).

164
00:15:16,385 --> 00:15:22,869
So, we're still talking about his virtues, so that’s his knowledge.

165
00:15:24,219 --> 00:15:30,844
His Deen(دِيْن) In Sahih al-Muslim(صحيح المسلم) Rasool Allah ﷺ have said,

166
00:15:30,883 --> 00:15:32,158
while I was asleep

167
00:15:32,249 --> 00:15:36,154
and you we find that Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), Rasool Allah ﷺ was seeing Umar(عمر) in many dreams.

168
00:15:37,131 --> 00:15:38,478
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying;

169
00:15:40,051 --> 00:15:45,451
بَيْنَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ رَأيْتُ النَّاسَ يُعْرَضُونَ وَعَلَيْهِمْ قُمُصٌ

170
00:15:45,944 --> 00:15:49,832
مِنْهَا ما يَبْلُغُ الثَّدْيَ، وَمِنْهَا مَا يَبْلُغُ دُوْنَ ذَلِكَ

171
00:15:50,623 --> 00:15:55,575
وَمَرَّةْ  عُمَرُ ابْنُ الخَطَّابِ وَعَلَيْهِ قَمِيْصٌ يَجُرُّهُ

172
00:15:56,349 --> 00:15:59,645
 قَالُوْا: مَا ذَ أَوَّلْتَ ذلِكَ؟ يَا رَسول الله  قَالَ:  الدِّينَ

173
00:16:00,269 --> 00:16:04,594
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: while I was asleep, people were being presented to me.

174
00:16:04,673 --> 00:16:06,418
They were walking in front of me.

175
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:14,070
 And they were wearing clothes, some of them had short clothes, some of them had long clothes.

176
00:16:14,904 --> 00:16:17,774
Some of them, their clothes would only reached to their chest.

177
00:16:18,232 --> 00:16:20,843
And some of them would have clothes, shorter than that.

178
00:16:23,161 --> 00:16:25,715
But then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) passed in front of me

179
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:30,171
and his clothes were so long that they were dragging on the floor.

180
00:16:33,355 --> 00:16:34,524
Is that a good sign or bad sign?

181
00:16:36,231 --> 00:16:39,028
You know we know in Sunnah(سنة) you are not suppose to have your clothes dragging.

182
00:16:41,817 --> 00:16:44,774
The Sunnah(سنة) is to have your clothes above the ankle.

183
00:16:45,364 --> 00:16:50,889
And here Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه is dragging his clothes behind him, way below the ankle.

184
00:16:52,661 --> 00:16:56,245
Well, because it’s a dream and dreams needs to be interpreted.

185
00:16:57,293 --> 00:17:00,082
They asked Rasool Allah ﷺ what is the interpretation of the dream?

186
00:17:00,332 --> 00:17:03,151
He said, I interpret that to mean that "Religion".

187
00:17:04,905 --> 00:17:07,862
So, the clothes were representing the religion of people.

188
00:17:08,217 --> 00:17:12,785
Some of them, that their religion was so short that it only reaches to their chest.

189
00:17:13,731 --> 00:17:18,369
While the Deen(دِيْن) of Umar(عمر) was dragging behind him, it was so great.

190
00:17:18,774 --> 00:17:24,664
His religion was so encompassing that it was covering his whole body and dragging on the ground.

191
00:17:25,752 --> 00:17:28,639
That’s the deen of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه .

192
00:17:31,450 --> 00:17:32,462
An-Nawwawi(النووي) says;

193
00:17:32,496 --> 00:17:36,105
قَالَ اَهْلُ الْعِبَارَةْ اَلْقَمِيْصُ فِى النَّوْمَ اَلدِّيْن

194
00:17:36,599 --> 00:17:40,691
وَجَرُّهُ يَدُلُّ عَلى بَقَاءِ آثَارَهِ الْجَمِيْلَةْ

195
00:17:41,303 --> 00:17:45,027
وَ سُنَّتَهُ الُحَسَنَهْ فِيْ الْمُسْلِمِيُنَ بَعْدَ وَفَاتِهْ لِيُقْتَضَى بِهْ

196
00:17:45,543 --> 00:17:51,028
An-Nawwawi(النووي) says; "that the scholars of interpreting dreams say, that

197
00:17:52,378 --> 00:17:59,003
clothes in dream means religion and when the clothes are dragging behind you,

198
00:17:59,315 --> 00:18:08,284
it means that your religious teachings will stay behind you and benefit the people.

199
00:18:09,049 --> 00:18:10,987
So, when his clothes are dragging behind him,

200
00:18:11,229 --> 00:18:15,073
it means that his teachings are gonna stay behind him for a long time.

201
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:17,461
And people are going to benefit from them.

202
00:18:19,817 --> 00:18:26,419
Another virtue of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه and this is in Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري).

203
00:18:30,888 --> 00:18:35,260
There were some women from Quraish(قريش), who were with Rasool Allah ﷺ

204
00:18:38,764 --> 00:18:43,416
and they were asking him, so many questions and their voices were loud.

205
00:18:44,531 --> 00:18:45,711
The Hadith(حديث) says;

206
00:18:46,427 --> 00:18:50,385
يُكَلِّمْنَه’وَيَسْتَكْفِرْنَه’عَالِيَةٌ أَصْوَاتُهُنْ

207
00:18:50,913 --> 00:18:55,870
They are asking him, and they are asking him a lot and their voices were loud.

208
00:18:58,005 --> 00:19:00,609
And then comes Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه .

209
00:19:01,895 --> 00:19:06,556
The women go into hiding, and they are suddenly mute, you dont hear a word.

210
00:19:08,627 --> 00:19:11,130
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) came in Rasool Allah ﷺ was laughing,

211
00:19:12,579 --> 00:19:15,486
 Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرإبن خطاب) said: Why are you laughing, O Messenger of Allah?

212
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:17,942
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Because of these women,

213
00:19:18,626 --> 00:19:22,491
their voices were very loud and they were asking me, so many questions and, when you come in,

214
00:19:22,946 --> 00:19:26,362
they suddenly go into hiding and they are quiet.

215
00:19:29,743 --> 00:19:33,693
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: O Messenger of Allah they should be respecting you,

216
00:19:34,408 --> 00:19:36,190
and then he goes to these women and says,

217
00:19:36,252 --> 00:19:37,469
"يَاعَدُّوَّاتْ اَنْفُسِهِنْ"

218
00:19:37,854 --> 00:19:39,510
"You enemy of yourselves".

219
00:19:40,385 --> 00:19:46,631
You are raising your voices in the presence of Allah, and you fear me, more than you fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.

220
00:19:46,885 --> 00:19:47,483
 They said: Yes!

221
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,218
نَعَمْ، أَنْتَ أَفَظُّ وَأَغْلَظْ

222
00:19:49,242 --> 00:19:51,855
Yes! Because you are harsh, and rough.

223
00:19:53,648 --> 00:19:55,195
They said: You are harsh and rough.

224
00:19:56,408 --> 00:20:00,579
Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed and said: O Umar(عمر)

225
00:20:00,936 --> 00:20:08,304
أيْهَ لَّكَ يَا اِبْنَ الْخَطَابْ مَا رَأَكَ الشَّيْطَانُ سَألِكًا فَجًا إِلَّا سَلَكَ فَجًا آخَرْ

226
00:20:08,813 --> 00:20:14,686
O Umar(عُمَر), whenever Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) sees you taking a road, he would take another road.

227
00:20:15,591 --> 00:20:18,425
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) cannot come in your path.

228
00:20:20,227 --> 00:20:21,221
Two points on this Hadith(حديث):

229
00:20:21,245 --> 00:20:26,592
NUMBER One, Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalaani(ابن حجر العسقلاني) he says, this doesn’t mean that Umar(عُمَر) is infallible,

230
00:20:27,001 --> 00:20:30,008
it doesn’t mean that Umar(عُمَر) is not exposed to the Waswasah(وسوسة) of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

231
00:20:30,528 --> 00:20:34,657
But it means that, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) has no way into Umar(عُمَر).

232
00:20:35,596 --> 00:20:38,565
And that Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) has hard time in dealing with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

233
00:20:38,955 --> 00:20:41,197
And that Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) fears Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

234
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:48,878
The Second point: And you will see this, whenever we are talking about the Seerah(سيرة) or the lives of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

235
00:20:52,401 --> 00:20:57,695
its relating to the interaction between men and the women

236
00:20:58,766 --> 00:21:06,654
and the culture of the women in that time, how was it in Madina?

237
00:21:07,279 --> 00:21:10,509
How was the life of women in Madina-Tu-Rasool Allah ﷺ?

238
00:21:11,059 --> 00:21:24,424
I think it's fair to say, that the women of Madina or the society of Madina was more conservative than the liberal Muslims today.

239
00:21:25,371 --> 00:21:28,756
And it's more liberal then the conservative Muslims of today.

240
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:32,006
You would find that it's somewhere in between.

241
00:21:33,366 --> 00:21:37,660
There was interaction between men and the women, they would speak

242
00:21:37,964 --> 00:21:42,664
the voice of women was not seen as Awrah(عورة) as we see in this Hadith(حديث).

243
00:21:42,689 --> 00:21:46,378
They were talking with Rasool Allah ﷺ  not only talking with him, but their voices were loud.

244
00:21:47,454 --> 00:21:53,874
And they would ask him and Rasool Allah ﷺ would give, would devote an entire session for the women, on weekly basis

245
00:21:54,197 --> 00:21:57,795
because they came to him and they said, that the men are taking all of your time what about us?

246
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:01,016
So Rasool Allah ﷺ devoted some special time for the women

247
00:22:01,548 --> 00:22:05,237
and, the women would also attend the sessions with the men.

248
00:22:05,288 --> 00:22:06,898
So, they ended up in getting a good deal.

249
00:22:07,202 --> 00:22:11,615
Because they would also attend the Halaqat(حلقات) of Rasool Allahﷺ in the Masjid(مسجد).

250
00:22:12,188 --> 00:22:17,314
They used to attend them in Musalla(مصلى) there wasn’t a barrier in those days, they would pray behind the men.

251
00:22:17,596 --> 00:22:20,916
Women used to serve in the Walayem(ولائم), the invitations,

252
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:24,872
they participated in Jihad(جهاد) with Rasool Allah ﷺ ,

253
00:22:25,187 --> 00:22:33,675
so I think there is a lot to learn if we go back to history and study the qualities of the society of Rasool Allah ﷺ in those days.

254
00:22:33,991 --> 00:22:35,988
Again I think in my view,

255
00:22:36,222 --> 00:22:39,164
they were more conservative then the liberal Muslims of today

256
00:22:39,203 --> 00:22:41,439
and they were more liberal then the conservative Muslims are.

257
00:22:43,868 --> 00:22:47,496
And they would carry on with their lives with, Hishmah(حشمة) with modesty,

258
00:22:47,541 --> 00:22:52,717
and when they would be dealing with men they would be dealing with men in a formal way,

259
00:22:52,893 --> 00:22:57,033
it wasn’t in informal joking manner, it was in a formal way.

260
00:22:59,505 --> 00:23:09,265
So, we needs to avoid the extremes today of going into the feminist ideology or realm

261
00:23:09,664 --> 00:23:17,483
or going to this conservative realm of, where woman should stuck in that room not allowed to be seen by anyone, not to talk to anyone

262
00:23:17,772 --> 00:23:21,330
and not to learn anything and not to go to the Masjid(مسجد), not to not, not, not……

263
00:23:23,029 --> 00:23:29,720
we have to go back to the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and see, how the society was then?

264
00:23:31,715 --> 00:23:33,409
That is the "Ideal Society".

265
00:23:40,997 --> 00:23:46,598
Plus Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن ألخطاب) would go and give Naseeha(نصيحة) to the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

266
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:52,469
A brother was telling me, how a brother will feel today, if a brother goes and gives his wife a Naseeha(نصيحة).

267
00:23:54,847 --> 00:23:58,271
Obviously Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had his daughter as one of Umahaatul Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين)

268
00:23:58,963 --> 00:24:02,037
but he would also direct the talk to all of them.

269
00:24:08,659 --> 00:24:10,540
We've talked about his virtue of being,

270
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:12,900
 "مُلْهَمْ هَذِهِ الْاُمَّةْ, اَوْ مُحَدَّثْ"

271
00:24:13,668 --> 00:24:14,583
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

272
00:24:14,607 --> 00:24:18,424
لَقَدْ كَانَ فِيْمَا قَبْلَكُمْ مِنَّ الْأُمَمِ مُحَدَثُوْنْ،

273
00:24:19,116 --> 00:24:21,946
فَإِنْ يَّكُنْ فِيْ اُمَّتِي أَحَدٌ فَإِنَّه’ عُمَرْ

274
00:24:22,370 --> 00:24:25,366
Rasool Allah ﷺ  said, there were Muhadasoon(محدثون) in the nations before you

275
00:24:25,706 --> 00:24:30,191
and if there is going to be Muhaddas(محدث) in my Ummah(امة), it would be Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه .

276
00:24:31,145 --> 00:24:37,740
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was also seen in another dream by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

277
00:24:37,815 --> 00:24:39,675
an amazing dream and this is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ),

278
00:24:41,322 --> 00:24:45,142
narrated by Abi Hurairah رضي الله عنه , Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

279
00:24:46,089 --> 00:24:51,287
while I was asleep, I saw that I was drawing water from a well.

280
00:24:51,311 --> 00:24:53,656
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was drawing water in this bucket

281
00:24:55,744 --> 00:25:06,762
and then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) came after me and he drew out water once or twice and his drawing was weak, May Allah forgive him.

282
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:09,650
when Rasool Allah ﷺ saying here is, May Allah forgive him,

283
00:25:09,713 --> 00:25:14,308
he is not criticizing Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), he is making a Dua(دُعَا) for him, May Allah forgive him.

284
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:22,082
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) he withdrew water once or twice but it was weak.

285
00:25:23,430 --> 00:25:29,081
And then Umar(عُمَر) came and he withdrew water and he was so strong.

286
00:25:29,464 --> 00:25:32,151
فَلَمْ أَرَ عَبْقَّرِيْ يَفْرِيْ فَرِيَهْ

287
00:25:32,478 --> 00:25:37,690
I haven’t seen a master, who was giving out water like him

288
00:25:38,666 --> 00:25:46,472
until all of the people left and they were full and their animals too, water was going left and right.

289
00:25:46,926 --> 00:25:51,086
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was strong he was just drawing bucket after another

290
00:25:51,287 --> 00:25:53,041
and pouring it and feeding the people.

291
00:25:56,021 --> 00:25:57,820
What's the interpretation of this dream?

292
00:25:58,942 --> 00:26:05,728
The scholars look back at our history and say this dream is talking about the Khilafah(خلافه).

293
00:26:07,807 --> 00:26:11,334
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the one, who was running the affairs of Muslims,

294
00:26:11,609 --> 00:26:13,296
so he was the one, giving them water.

295
00:26:14,713 --> 00:26:22,562
And then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) came after him and he was giving the people water but Rasool Allah ﷺ said it was weak

296
00:26:22,792 --> 00:26:23,481
 why?

297
00:26:23,698 --> 00:26:28,434
Because Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was little over two years a very short time,

298
00:26:30,386 --> 00:26:35,483
but then Umar(عُمَر) came in and his Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was long ten plus(10 +)

299
00:26:36,502 --> 00:26:38,994
and that was the, golden era of Islam.

300
00:26:40,104 --> 00:26:45,901
That was when the blessings came down on the Ummah(امة) in terms of knowledge,

301
00:26:46,345 --> 00:26:51,607
in terms of spreading of knowledge, in terms of the Futohaat(فتوحات), the conquests,

302
00:26:52,172 --> 00:26:57,597
also even when it comes to worldly aspects, the administration of the Ummah(أمة)

303
00:26:57,859 --> 00:27:05,615
and the institutions and the wealth wise the Muslims, they were becoming very wealthy.

304
00:27:07,232 --> 00:27:11,368
So, this Hadith(حديث) is talking about the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

305
00:27:11,624 --> 00:27:17,359
And Abqari(عبقري), the word Abqari(عبقري), which was the description that Rasool Allah ﷺ gave to Umar(عُمَر).

306
00:27:17,683 --> 00:27:23,167
Today it means, Genius but it also means Master or Leader, Noble man.

307
00:27:27,822 --> 00:27:29,008
In another dream;

308
00:27:29,850 --> 00:27:38,528
and brothers and sisters you see that dreams played an important role in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

309
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:41,307
Rasool Allah ﷺ for example after Saalat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر)

310
00:27:41,575 --> 00:27:45,350
he would turn around and he would ask the Sahabah(صحابه) did any of you have see a dream?

311
00:27:45,958 --> 00:27:48,664
And they would narrate their dream and he would interpret dreams for them

312
00:27:48,689 --> 00:27:50,825
and sometimes Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) would interpret the dream.

313
00:27:51,384 --> 00:27:57,050
So the dreams are Mubashiraat(مبشّرات) they are glad tidings that Allah gives to this Ummah(امة).

314
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:03,378
So, the early Muslims use to talk about the dreams, they would talk about Al-Fittan(ألفتن)

315
00:28:03,402 --> 00:28:05,910
they would talk about the events of end of time.

316
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:11,286
This is not like something that you are not suppose to involve in

317
00:28:11,516 --> 00:28:15,124
obviously but these things need to follow the criteria of Sharia’a(شريعة)

318
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:21,522
and for example, if somebody comes and says in a dream that I have seen a dream

319
00:28:22,130 --> 00:28:24,133
where voice told me not to pray anymore.

320
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:29,824
You see, dreams do not change the Sharia’a(شريعه).

321
00:28:30,606 --> 00:28:33,308
Dreams do not make Halal(حلال) Haram(حرام) or Haram(حرام) Halal(حلال).

322
00:28:33,922 --> 00:28:37,226
Dreams are Mubashiraat(مبشّرات), they are good news glad tidings for you.

323
00:28:38,261 --> 00:28:41,482
Because sometimes Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) comes to people and deceives them like that.

324
00:28:45,991 --> 00:28:54,972
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "In my dream, I visited Jannah(جنة)

325
00:28:55,904 --> 00:29:02,794
and I saw a Romessa(روميصه) a wife of Abu Talha(أبوطلحة), a woman from Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

326
00:29:03,808 --> 00:29:08,279
and then I heard footsteps, so I asked who it was?

327
00:29:08,717 --> 00:29:10,437
I was told this is Bilal(بلال)

328
00:29:12,245 --> 00:29:14,683
and then I came near to a beautiful palace

329
00:29:15,445 --> 00:29:19,005
and I saw a woman who was making a Wudu(وضوء) next to the palace.

330
00:29:19,924 --> 00:29:21,798
And I said who does this palace belongs to?

331
00:29:22,681 --> 00:29:25,522
I was told this palace belongs to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

332
00:29:26,847 --> 00:29:30,050
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I wanted to go into the palace and see it,

333
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:34,473
but then I remembered your jealousy, so I walked away.

334
00:29:35,780 --> 00:29:39,554
Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) cried and  said, O Rasool Ullah I would'nt be jealous of you.

335
00:29:44,174 --> 00:29:46,113
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was jealous that was his nature.

336
00:29:46,138 --> 00:29:51,186
He was very protective of his wives and daughters.

337
00:29:52,526 --> 00:29:56,289
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that, so that's why he didn’t want to go next to his palace

338
00:29:57,227 --> 00:30:01,163
and he said because of your jealousy I stayed away and Umar(عُمَر) cried

339
00:30:01,719 --> 00:30:04,561
and he said, not from you, O Messenger of Allah.

340
00:30:08,279 --> 00:30:10,939
What does it mean when a woman is making Wudu(وضؤ) outside of her palace?

341
00:30:10,964 --> 00:30:13,448
I mean there is no Salah(صلاة) in Jannah(جنة), so why would there be Wudu(وضؤ)?

342
00:30:14,685 --> 00:30:16,249
What's the point of making a Wudu(وضؤ) in Jannah(جنة)?

343
00:30:17,693 --> 00:30:24,519
So, this was the question posed by the scholars and An-Nawwawi(النووي) or Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر)

344
00:30:26,143 --> 00:30:28,810
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجر) actually, he said,

345
00:30:32,032 --> 00:30:39,854
Wudu(وضؤ) in Arabic, one of the derivates of it is Wadha'a(وَضَاءَةْ) which means beauty.

346
00:30:41,781 --> 00:30:46,778
So, this woman is making Wudu(وضؤ) in Jannah(جنة) to make herself more beautiful.

347
00:30:47,845 --> 00:30:50,646
So, every time she makes Wudu(وضؤ) she becomes more beautiful,

348
00:30:50,892 --> 00:30:52,948
every time she makes Wudu(وضؤ) she becomes more beautiful.

349
00:30:53,483 --> 00:30:56,335
So, Wudu(وضؤ) in Jannah(جنة) is not for worship, it's not for Salah(صلاة)

350
00:30:56,688 --> 00:31:01,442
but it's to add and increase to her beauty and that's why she was making Wudu(وضؤ).

351
00:31:08,970 --> 00:31:12,667
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه loved Rasool Allah ﷺ so much.

352
00:31:13,317 --> 00:31:17,430
In Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and says;

353
00:31:19,820 --> 00:31:24,179
لَأ اَنْتَ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍإِلَّا مِنْ نَفْسِيْ

354
00:31:24,947 --> 00:31:28,684
O Messenger of Allah, I love you more than everything.

355
00:31:29,276 --> 00:31:31,894
Now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very straight forward and honest.

356
00:31:32,583 --> 00:31:38,093
He said, O Messenger of Allah, I love you more than everything except myself.

357
00:31:41,114 --> 00:31:45,300
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, not until you love me more than yourself.

358
00:31:46,310 --> 00:31:53,049
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) comes back and says, O Messenger of Allah, Now I love you more than everything including myself.

359
00:31:53,382 --> 00:31:57,129
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Now you have attained the Faith.

360
00:31:58,409 --> 00:32:04,028
You have attained complete faith when you love Rasool Allah ﷺ more than everything including yourself.

361
00:32:05,399 --> 00:32:11,811
Now today our understanding of love is that it's an abstract feeling

362
00:32:11,836 --> 00:32:17,007
that you have in your heart and there is no implications to it.

363
00:32:17,867 --> 00:32:20,969
But that’s not how they used to understand love.

364
00:32:21,604 --> 00:32:24,506
For them love was a feeling and also it was an action.

365
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:32,247
For them when you love somebody, it means you would put them in a high esteem,

366
00:32:33,473 --> 00:32:37,750
you would think about them a lot, and when you love someone more than yourself

367
00:32:37,822 --> 00:32:40,935
it means that you will sacrifice yourself, for them.

368
00:32:42,203 --> 00:32:47,686
So, love was not a lip service it’s not what you say, it's not something that you claim you feel,

369
00:32:47,962 --> 00:32:49,297
 there are implications to it.

370
00:32:50,276 --> 00:32:52,720
When you are confronted with a situation,

371
00:32:53,283 --> 00:32:59,123
where you have to make a choice between your interests, and the person you love

372
00:33:00,118 --> 00:33:04,918
that is a test on whether you are more important, or the other person.

373
00:33:05,484 --> 00:33:07,844
So, if you love Rasool Allah ﷺ more than yourself

374
00:33:08,350 --> 00:33:12,581
and you are confronted with a situation, where you have to sacrifice for Rasool Allah ﷺ yourself,

375
00:33:13,507 --> 00:33:16,358
if you sacrifice yourself for Rasool Ullah that means you love him,

376
00:33:16,541 --> 00:33:19,588
if you don’t that means you really love yourself more.

377
00:33:22,683 --> 00:33:30,633
Now, we try to get away from the real implications of loving Rasool Allah ﷺ by praising him and reciting poetry

378
00:33:30,672 --> 00:33:34,209
 and feel good things to make us feel that we love him.

379
00:33:34,740 --> 00:33:39,724
And when we are put to the challenge time to really sacrifice for them, we bail out.

380
00:33:42,131 --> 00:33:43,812
If you love Rasool Allah ﷺ

381
00:33:44,183 --> 00:33:48,261
You would consider his Sunnah(سنة) to be more important than what the people think.

382
00:33:49,276 --> 00:33:54,304
You would consider his path to be more important than your own interests

383
00:33:55,242 --> 00:33:58,957
and when Rasool Allah ﷺ asks you in a Hadith(حديث) to do something,

384
00:33:59,226 --> 00:34:01,803
you will be willing to do it no matter what the consequences are?

385
00:34:03,096 --> 00:34:06,975
That’s how you prove your love of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

386
00:34:07,197 --> 00:34:08,631
It's not by singing songs about him.

387
00:34:11,432 --> 00:34:17,436
I am not saying praising Rasool Allah ﷺ is Haram(حرام), don’t get me wrong, sometimes people would jump to conclusions.

388
00:34:18,281 --> 00:34:24,730
I am just saying, that that might be an easy way out for you to feel good that you love Rasool Allah ﷺ.

389
00:34:27,941 --> 00:34:33,860
Making Salah(صلاة) on Rasool Allah ﷺ in the form of poetry or in form of Nasheeds(ناشيد) is absolutely fine

390
00:34:35,311 --> 00:34:39,562
but that’s not the criteria that proves whether you love him or not?

391
00:34:41,467 --> 00:34:46,129
It is the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ that proves that not only loving Rasool Allah ﷺ, if  you love Allah.

392
00:34:46,819 --> 00:34:48,289
 Allahعَزّ وجَلّ says;

393
00:34:48,322 --> 00:34:53,186
إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّونَ اللَّهَ فَاتَّبِعُونِي يُحْبِبْكُمُ اللَّهُ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ ۗ

394
00:34:53,714 --> 00:34:55,999
If you claim that you love Allah, in Surat Al-Imraan(سورة العمران),

395
00:34:56,288 --> 00:35:00,606
if you claim that you love Allah then follow the Messenger of Allah,

396
00:35:00,942 --> 00:35:03,565
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ will love you and forgive you.

397
00:35:06,184 --> 00:35:09,917
So, even if you want to show your love of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ

398
00:35:10,638 --> 00:35:13,274
you going to have to follow the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

399
00:35:14,599 --> 00:35:17,112
And when we talk about the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

400
00:35:17,526 --> 00:35:22,074
we just shouldn’t think about Sunnah(سنة) as the outward Sunnah(سنة) which is the part of the Sunnah(سنة)

401
00:35:22,439 --> 00:35:27,922
but also how did he live his life, what did he spend his time doing in Madina?

402
00:35:30,076 --> 00:35:32,972
Did he spend his time fighting the enemies of Allah?

403
00:35:33,284 --> 00:35:39,200
what did Rasool Allah ﷺ do, when he was in Madina?

404
00:35:39,852 --> 00:35:42,920
How did he spend those ten years?

405
00:35:44,316 --> 00:35:46,488
We should want to do the same, like he did.

406
00:35:47,254 --> 00:35:50,418
He spent his time in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

407
00:35:52,371 --> 00:35:56,063
teaching in the Masjid(مسجد), Qur’an and Hadith(حديث)

408
00:35:57,554 --> 00:36:00,786
and being an example for the Sahabah(صحابة) that’s how he spend his time?

409
00:36:01,505 --> 00:36:05,060
Being an example teaching and Fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

410
00:36:05,685 --> 00:36:07,697
That’s the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

411
00:36:07,742 --> 00:36:11,553
If you want to talk about Sunnah(سنة) this is the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله ولسلام عليه

412
00:36:19,345 --> 00:36:24,271
And Rasool Ullah loved Umar(عُمَر) a lot too, it's not just one way.

413
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:26,850
They both love each other

414
00:36:26,890 --> 00:36:33,233
Amr Ibn Aas رضي الله عنه, he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said who is the most beloved person to you?

415
00:36:35,346 --> 00:36:37,134
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "Ayesha(عائشه)"

416
00:36:39,455 --> 00:36:43,609
Amr(عمرو) said: What about among the men?

417
00:36:44,093 --> 00:36:46,425
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "Her father."

418
00:36:48,248 --> 00:36:49,704
Amr(عمرو) said: And then who?

419
00:36:50,006 --> 00:36:51,345
He ﷺ said: "Umar(عُمَر)".

420
00:36:53,373 --> 00:37:01,147
So Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) the most and then Umar(عمر) comes next.

421
00:37:05,725 --> 00:37:12,722
He was given glad tidings of Jannah(جنة) many times, one in Makkah,

422
00:37:12,867 --> 00:37:15,769
which is the Ten Asharat Al-Mubashiroon Fil Jannah(العشرة المبشرون بالجنة)

423
00:37:16,078 --> 00:37:18,266
but also in Madina happened more than once.

424
00:37:19,436 --> 00:37:22,677
Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting in Bier Al-Arees(بئرأريس),

425
00:37:23,647 --> 00:37:26,902
you would have a well, and a garden, and then it would be surrounded by a wall.

426
00:37:27,757 --> 00:37:31,736
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting on the rim of the well,

427
00:37:33,749 --> 00:37:36,944
they would also have a pool next to the well, they would draw water into this pool,

428
00:37:37,024 --> 00:37:42,010
so that you could come and drink immediately, you don’t have to withdraw water, so there would be a, small pool.

429
00:37:42,311 --> 00:37:46,779
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting with his feet in that pool,

430
00:37:47,621 --> 00:37:52,930
Abu Musa al-Ashari(ابو موسى العشعري) said: Today I am going to be the guard, for Rasool Allah ﷺ,

431
00:37:55,018 --> 00:38:03,902
 not guard him in terms of protection but, to make sure that nobody comes in, except when they seek permission, Istezaan(إستئذان).

432
00:38:06,067 --> 00:38:13,577
So, he sits on the gate and he hears somebody opening the gate,

433
00:38:14,322 --> 00:38:15,453
so he says; who is it?

434
00:38:15,537 --> 00:38:16,236
It was Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

435
00:38:16,556 --> 00:38:20,052
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and says, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is outside, should I allow him in?

436
00:38:21,392 --> 00:38:24,459
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! Wa-Bashshir Ho Bil Jannah(وبشره بالجنة),

437
00:38:25,227 --> 00:38:26,901
yes and give him glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

438
00:38:27,234 --> 00:38:29,326
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) comes in and he says Al-Hamdolillah(الحمد لله)

439
00:38:30,181 --> 00:38:33,469
and then he sits next to Rasool Ullah on his right,

440
00:38:34,884 --> 00:38:40,194
and then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) comes and he opens the gate Abu Musa(ابو موسى) goes and he asks for permission

441
00:38:40,741 --> 00:38:44,254
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allow him in, Wa-Bashshir Ho Bil Jannah(وبشره بالجنة).

442
00:38:44,778 --> 00:38:46,857
So Umar(عُمَر) was given glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

443
00:38:46,913 --> 00:38:50,579
and he said: Al-Hamdolillah(الحمد لله) and he sat to the left of Rasool Allah ﷺ

444
00:38:52,373 --> 00:38:57,749
and then Uthman(عثمان) comes, so Abu Musa(ابو موسى) asks permission for him,

445
00:38:58,469 --> 00:39:00,529
so Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allow him in,

446
00:39:01,041 --> 00:39:03,538
وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةْ ، عَلى بَلْوَى تُصِيْبُهْ

447
00:39:04,698 --> 00:39:12,171
Give him the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة), and that calamity will befall him.

448
00:39:14,711 --> 00:39:17,241
So, Uthman(عثمان) comes in and he says; Al-Hamdolillah(الحمد لله)

449
00:39:17,851 --> 00:39:19,782
and then he says; Allah Ho Must'aan(الله المستعان).

450
00:39:20,922 --> 00:39:24,278
Praise be to Allah and then he said, Allah Ho Must'aan(الله المستعان),

451
00:39:24,772 --> 00:39:26,928
Allah is the One, Who give me help.

452
00:39:27,655 --> 00:39:31,466
Because there was a glad tidings and there was also a warning.

453
00:39:32,249 --> 00:39:33,665
A calamity will befall you

454
00:39:34,329 --> 00:39:41,548
 and this might have been referring to the Fitnah(فتنة) that happened at the end of his Khilafah(خِلَافَه), which ended with his own death.

455
00:39:43,343 --> 00:39:50,769
Uthman(عثمان) came in and there was no place next to Rasool Ullah to sit, so he ended up sitting in front of them.

456
00:39:52,460 --> 00:39:57,101
Saeed Ibn Musayyib(سعيد ابن مصيَّب) says; I interpret that, to mean, their Graves.

457
00:39:58,568 --> 00:40:03,153
Rasool Allah ﷺ had Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), and Umar(عُمَر) sitting next to him, and that’s where, they were buried.

458
00:40:03,678 --> 00:40:07,107
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) there was no place for him, so he was buried in Al-Baqiyyah(البقيه).

459
00:40:18,402 --> 00:40:20,454
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was ill,

460
00:40:20,479 --> 00:40:26,066
and this was the illness that ended with His death, (صلوات الله وسلام عليه).

461
00:40:26,813 --> 00:40:32,434
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) to have somebody lead the prayer.

462
00:40:32,588 --> 00:40:36,789
Rasool Allah ﷺ according to this narration, have somebody lead the prayer.

463
00:40:38,713 --> 00:40:40,951
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not specify Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

464
00:40:42,948 --> 00:40:49,059
Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) didn’t find Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), so he told Umar(عُمَر) to lead the Salah(صلاة),

465
00:40:52,033 --> 00:40:53,574
the voice of Umar(عُمَر) was loud.

466
00:40:53,727 --> 00:40:56,576
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ  heard it, in Salah(صلاة), he said:

467
00:40:56,642 --> 00:41:00,703
يَأْبَى اللهُ ذَلِكَ وَالْمُسْلِمُوْنَ

468
00:41:01,727 --> 00:41:09,575
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ rejects that, and the Muslims reject that, and Rasool Allah ﷺ repeated it again.

469
00:41:10,400 --> 00:41:12,613
مُرُوْا اَبَا بَكَرْ فَلَيُصَلِيْ بِالنَّاسْ

470
00:41:12,722 --> 00:41:14,988
Tell Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) to lead the Salah(صلاة).

471
00:41:15,937 --> 00:41:21,270
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying, that it is not pleasing to Allah and the Muslims

472
00:41:21,315 --> 00:41:23,907
to have Umar(عُمَر) lead the Salah(صلاة), when Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is around.

473
00:41:24,694 --> 00:41:26,338
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) should be the one leading the Salah(صلاة).

474
00:41:27,263 --> 00:41:29,995
So, when Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) came back, he was one leading the Salah(صلاة).

475
00:41:30,487 --> 00:41:32,213
Umar(عُمَر) went to Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) and said:

476
00:41:32,238 --> 00:41:34,922
"Woe to you Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه)! why did you do that, to me?

477
00:41:35,731 --> 00:41:40,517
when you told me to lead the Salah(صلاة) I thought Rasool Ullah told you, to tell me to lead the Salah(صلاة),

478
00:41:41,497 --> 00:41:44,048
if that wasn’t the case, I wouldn't have lead the Salah(صلاة).

479
00:41:44,716 --> 00:41:48,716
Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) said, Rasool Allah ﷺ  did not tell me, to tell you to lead the Salah(صلاة),

480
00:41:49,044 --> 00:41:55,242
but when I didn’t find Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), I saw you as the most appropriate person to lead the Salah(صلاة).

481
00:41:57,490 --> 00:41:59,371
So, there are two things to learn from this Hadith(حديث):

482
00:42:00,611 --> 00:42:01,331
Number one:

483
00:42:01,535 --> 00:42:05,052
Rasool Allah, did not specify to Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) to have Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) lead the Salah(صلاة).

484
00:42:05,077 --> 00:42:08,183
Nevertheless, Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) understood that it means Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

485
00:42:09,190 --> 00:42:12,689
Which sends a very clear message, that for the Muslim community,

486
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:15,149
it was clear to them the Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is their leader.

487
00:42:16,594 --> 00:42:18,264
That he is the one, who should be the Imam(إمام).

488
00:42:20,014 --> 00:42:21,053
That’s number one.

489
00:42:22,645 --> 00:42:23,689
Number two:

490
00:42:24,429 --> 00:42:31,379
Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه) made a judgment, that if Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is not aroundthen the one, who should be Imam(اِمَام) in his absence is Umar(عُمَر).

491
00:42:31,911 --> 00:42:36,171
So, according to Ibn Zama’a(ابن ضمعه), the second in command is Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

492
00:42:36,794 --> 00:42:41,898
And for Muslims, position of the Imamah(اِمَامه) of Salah(صلاة) is more important than leading them in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) affairs.

493
00:42:42,614 --> 00:42:45,049
Because the Imam(اِمَام) of Salah(صلاة) is Imam(اِمَام) in Deen(دِيْن)

494
00:42:45,318 --> 00:42:47,424
 and for them Deen(دِيْن) was more important than Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

495
00:42:48,309 --> 00:42:51,116
So, if they would appoint somebody to lead them in Deen(دِيْن),

496
00:42:52,162 --> 00:42:55,036
- it's obvious that he would also have that person lead them in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

497
00:42:55,060 --> 00:42:57,645
because for them Deen(دِيْن) was higher than Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

498
00:43:00,575 --> 00:43:07,678
And this is one of the many evidences or indications that the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) starts with Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and then Umar(عُمَر).

499
00:43:10,151 --> 00:43:11,971
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away,

500
00:43:13,127 --> 00:43:15,069
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) wasn’t around he was in the As-Sanhh(اَلصَّنْح),

501
00:43:15,196 --> 00:43:18,591
one of his wives was in As-Sanhh(اَلصَّنْح) which was close to Madina.

502
00:43:19,355 --> 00:43:21,864
So, he was not present when Rasool Allah ﷺ was passed away.

503
00:43:23,065 --> 00:43:31,005
The news spread and it was the greatest catastrophe that the Sahabah(صحابه) every experienced.

504
00:43:32,197 --> 00:43:39,410
I mean, you will not be able to understand and to appreciate what the Sahabah(صحابه) went through?

505
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:41,594
Because for them Rasool Ullah was everything.

506
00:43:44,239 --> 00:43:52,607
The Sahabah(صحابه) would go back home to their wives and children and then they would feel home sick.

507
00:43:54,162 --> 00:43:55,956
They are at home and they are feeling home sick.

508
00:43:57,147 --> 00:44:02,236
Because they want to go back to their real home, the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

509
00:44:04,335 --> 00:44:08,772
And they would say, we would be completely different people when we are in your presence Rasool Allah ﷺ.

510
00:44:09,985 --> 00:44:13,543
One of the Sahabah(صحابه) said, Nafaqa Hunzala(نافق حنظلة) I am a hypocrite,

511
00:44:14,212 --> 00:44:15,817
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, why would you say that?

512
00:44:16,127 --> 00:44:22,456
He said, because Messenger of Allah when I am with you, I feel in my heart to be closest to Allah

513
00:44:22,515 --> 00:44:29,964
and then when I go back home, and blend in with my kids and my family I feel different.

514
00:44:31,128 --> 00:44:36,440
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, first of all he told him that it's not a Nifaaq(نفاق)

515
00:44:37,470 --> 00:44:48,766
and then he told him, if you would carry on, on the same state you are in, when you are with me,

516
00:44:50,204 --> 00:44:53,387
the angels would come and shake your hands in the streets of Madina

517
00:44:55,641 --> 00:44:57,316
but it's, As-Sa'a, Was'Sa'a(ساعة و ساعة الله)

518
00:44:57,446 --> 00:45:01,659
one hour for Allah and one hour for yourself and an hour for your family.

519
00:45:02,657 --> 00:45:04,679
That’s the destiny of Allah for us as human.

520
00:45:05,539 --> 00:45:07,175
You have to split your time up.

521
00:45:07,711 --> 00:45:12,073
Sometimes, has to go to work, sometimes has to go to family, sometimes has to go to Ibadah(عبادة).

522
00:45:12,657 --> 00:45:24,833
You can’t have it all, going in one area, this Rahbaniyyah(رهبانية) life in monasteries is not something that is approved in Islam.

523
00:45:28,747 --> 00:45:39,662
So, it was a shock for Sahabah(صحابه) some of them just sat down and couldn’t move, like Uthman(عثمان) he couldn’t speak.

524
00:45:39,819 --> 00:45:43,230
 That’s it, he sat down and couldn’t speak, he couldn’t anything helpless.

525
00:45:46,904 --> 00:45:54,675
While Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was carrying his sword, roaming around then he went to the Masjid(مسجد)

526
00:45:55,332 --> 00:45:57,941
and he stands up and he gives a speech.

527
00:45:58,995 --> 00:46:04,178
He says: "There are some Munafiqeen(منافقين), who are claiming that Rasool Allah ﷺ died,

528
00:46:05,084 --> 00:46:10,878
 Rasool Allah ﷺ did not die, but he went to meet Allah, like Musa(موسى) went to meet Allah.

529
00:46:12,619 --> 00:46:19,005
And when Musa(موسى) went to meet Allah for forty days, Bannu Israel(بنو اسرائيل) said, that he died but then he came back.

530
00:46:19,449 --> 00:46:22,176
 And Rasool Allah ﷺ will came back like Musa(موسى) came back.

531
00:46:22,757 --> 00:46:28,854
And Rasool Allah ﷺ will cut off the hands and feet of the people who claim that he died.

532
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:33,118
And he was saying, anybody who is saying that Muhammad(محمد) is dead,

533
00:46:33,505 --> 00:46:35,108
I am going to behead him with this sword.

534
00:46:37,817 --> 00:46:42,102
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), his heart could not handle it, could not believe that Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

535
00:46:43,610 --> 00:46:45,441
That was how difficult it was on them.

536
00:46:45,965 --> 00:46:53,763
A strong man like Umar(عُمَر) for him to be shaken, in such a way,  it tells you that Rasool Allah ﷺ meant everything to him.

537
00:46:54,829 --> 00:46:59,138
Because he was not feeble, weak human being,

538
00:46:59,452 --> 00:47:03,506
he was very, very strong man who had control over his emotions.

539
00:47:04,053 --> 00:47:07,890
So, that shows you how dear Rasool Allah ﷺ was to Umar(عُمَر).

540
00:47:09,507 --> 00:47:12,007
His heart was telling him don’t believe it,

541
00:47:14,670 --> 00:47:17,497
and his emotions overwhelmed his mind.

542
00:47:19,940 --> 00:47:26,058
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) came back on his horse, he went straight to the house of Rasool Ullah.

543
00:47:26,711 --> 00:47:29,045
Rasool Allah ﷺ died, on the lap of Ayesha(عائشه),

544
00:47:30,739 --> 00:47:37,020
so he uncovers Rasool Allah ﷺ and then he kisses him and cries, and then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) says,

545
00:47:37,889 --> 00:47:42,651
The death, that was destined for you has passed, you will never die again

546
00:47:44,917 --> 00:47:49,778
And then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) goes to the Masjid(مسجد), while Umar(عُمَر) is speaking,

547
00:47:51,110 --> 00:47:53,164
telling the people that Muhammad(محمد) did not die.

548
00:47:54,556 --> 00:47:59,100
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said, to Umar(عُمَر); stay quiet!.

549
00:48:00,281 --> 00:48:04,967
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was not listening, he was carrying on!

550
00:48:05,914 --> 00:48:10,559
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) ignored him, and stood aside and started speaking.

551
00:48:11,391 --> 00:48:15,120
So, when people saw Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) speaking they left Umar(عُمَر) and they came to him.

552
00:48:17,507 --> 00:48:22,564
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in a very short and very brief speech, he said:

553
00:48:23,975 --> 00:48:31,368
مَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ مُحَمَّدَ، فَإِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا قَدْ مَاتَ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ حَيٌّ لاَ يَمُوتُ،

554
00:48:32,169 --> 00:48:38,846
وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِكُمْ

555
00:48:39,127 --> 00:48:42,281
وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَى عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئًا

556
00:48:43,674 --> 00:48:47,185
Whoever, was worshiping Muhammad(محمد), Muhammad(محمد) is dead

557
00:48:48,400 --> 00:48:52,773
and whoever, was worshiping Allah, Allah is alive and never dies,

558
00:48:53,508 --> 00:48:56,445
and then he recites to them, an Ayah(آية) from Surah Al-Imran(سورة العمران)

559
00:48:56,617 --> 00:48:58,873
that Muhammad(محمد) is but a messenger,

560
00:49:00,847 --> 00:49:04,563
if he dies, or he is killed are you going to go back on your heels?

561
00:49:07,173 --> 00:49:11,153
Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) said: As if we heard that verse for the first time.

562
00:49:13,047 --> 00:49:15,908
When Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) narrated that verse to us

563
00:49:16,182 --> 00:49:20,104
we all went around reciting that verse and carrying it to the people.

564
00:49:26,441 --> 00:49:33,058
And then there was the important event of choosing the Khalifah(خليفه).

565
00:49:36,986 --> 00:49:41,639
The Sahabah(صحابه) were discussing it, even before they buried the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

566
00:49:42,938 --> 00:49:47,208
Rasool Ullah passed away on Monday and he was buried on Wednesday.

567
00:49:48,242 --> 00:49:53,347
Now, we know the Sunnah(سنة) is to speed up the burial process.

568
00:49:55,068 --> 00:49:58,120
The Sunnah(سنة) is to bury the deceased as fast as possible.

569
00:49:59,201 --> 00:50:03,531
Rasool Allah ﷺ his Janazah(جنازه) was delayed for two days,

570
00:50:03,700 --> 00:50:07,268
he died on Monday and he was buried on Wednesday why?

571
00:50:07,575 --> 00:50:10,856
Because Sahabah(صحابه) were busy in discussing the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

572
00:50:13,585 --> 00:50:15,643
Saeed Ibn Musayyib(سعيد ابن مصيَّب) was asked about this,

573
00:50:15,667 --> 00:50:21,230
I mean, how come they neglect the Janazah(جنازه) and discussing this issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه)?

574
00:50:21,841 --> 00:50:27,417
Some people today might say what, that they were so busy with politics they leave the Sunnah(سنة) of Janazah(جنازه)?

575
00:50:27,859 --> 00:50:29,160
Saeed Ibn Musayyib(سعيد ابن مصيَّب) said:

576
00:50:30,324 --> 00:50:31,024
كَرِه،

577
00:50:31,532 --> 00:50:37,573
"The Sahabah(صحابه) didn’t want to be outside of the Jamma’a(جماعة) for even part of a day."

578
00:50:39,610 --> 00:50:42,527
living in a Jamma’a(جماعة) was so important to the Sahabah(صحابه)

579
00:50:42,844 --> 00:50:47,942
they did not want a day to pass by, without them, being in a Jamma’a(جماعة), with an Ameer(امير)

580
00:50:48,413 --> 00:50:50,277
because you cannot have a Jamma’a(جماعة) without Ameer(امير),

581
00:50:50,553 --> 00:50:52,313
- there is no Jamma’a(جماعة) without Ameer(امير).

582
00:50:52,937 --> 00:50:55,638
So they had to sort out who will be the Ameer(امير) first.

583
00:50:56,710 --> 00:51:03,123
And the fact that they put that in a greater priority then the burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ tells you

584
00:51:03,170 --> 00:51:07,735
 that their understanding was that the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was critical

585
00:51:10,010 --> 00:51:12,841
and they delayed the Janazah(جنازه) to discuss that.

586
00:51:17,563 --> 00:51:24,753
The Ansaar(أنْصَار) were discussing, appointing the Ameer(امير) from within their ranks.

587
00:51:25,804 --> 00:51:30,108
So, the news reaches to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), Umar(عُمَر) and Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة),

588
00:51:30,686 --> 00:51:34,745
so the three men rush to Saqeefat Banu Sa’ada(ثَقِيْفَةْ بَنُو سَعْدَه),

589
00:51:35,584 --> 00:51:39,899
the portico, a shed that belong to Banu Sa’ada(بنو سعده).

590
00:51:40,653 --> 00:51:45,258
The Ansaar(أنْصَار) were meeting under it, and they were discussing this issue.

591
00:51:46,044 --> 00:51:49,436
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), Umar(عُمَر), and Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة) rushed in.

592
00:51:51,339 --> 00:51:54,378
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I have already prepared a speech.

593
00:51:55,674 --> 00:52:02,216
I already worked out a speech in my mind of some important points that need to be said,

594
00:52:03,501 --> 00:52:09,957
so I stand up and I want to speak and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) stops me and he starts speaking.

595
00:52:13,030 --> 00:52:19,943
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said there was nothing that I wanted to say that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) did not say and he added more to it.

596
00:52:21,571 --> 00:52:25,806
Umar(عُمَر) said the whole point of me, preparing a speech was so that

597
00:52:26,453 --> 00:52:32,074
because may be Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was shy of saying something may be, he miss something, so I wanted to do it for him.

598
00:52:33,033 --> 00:52:34,895
 He ended up saying it and more.

599
00:52:36,103 --> 00:52:37,990
He said, I couldn’t have done better than that.

600
00:52:40,705 --> 00:52:47,983
The just of it, was that the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) should be among the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون).

601
00:52:49,093 --> 00:52:51,660
Which are the core group of Daw'ah(دعوة).

602
00:52:52,999 --> 00:52:56,709
The Ansaar(أنْصَار) had the different understanding that since they are the helpers,

603
00:52:56,734 --> 00:52:58,973
 they are the one who assisted Rasool Allah ﷺ

604
00:52:59,343 --> 00:53:03,448
they should be the leaders, plus this is their town, this is their land.

605
00:53:04,905 --> 00:53:08,849
And they were planning to appoint Sa’ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عباده) to be the Ameer(امير).

606
00:53:09,880 --> 00:53:15,335
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told Sa’ad(سعد); Sa'ad(سعد) did you remember one day, we were sitting with Rasool Allah ﷺ

607
00:53:15,375 --> 00:53:17,825
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said, that Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is in Quraish(قريش).

608
00:53:18,428 --> 00:53:19,452
Do you remember that?

609
00:53:19,754 --> 00:53:22,010
Sa’ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عباده) said: Yes! I do remember that.

610
00:53:25,111 --> 00:53:26,970
So, he reminded him with that Hadith(حديث)

611
00:53:27,349 --> 00:53:32,693
and there were some discussions went on for example this suggestion by Al-Hubaab Bin Munzir(الحباب ابن مُنْذر).

612
00:53:32,863 --> 00:53:34,475
مِنَّا اَمِيْر وَمِنْكُمْ اَمِيْر

613
00:53:34,698 --> 00:53:36,953
Let's have one Ameer(امير) from us and one Ameer(امير) from you.

614
00:53:37,316 --> 00:53:41,002
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You cannot have two Ameer(امير)'s in one house.

615
00:53:44,034 --> 00:53:52,471
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) to bring an end to this discussion that could end up causing Fitnah(فتنة).

616
00:53:54,033 --> 00:54:02,999
He said: Give Bay’ah(بيعة) to these two men, Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(ابو عبيده عمرو بن جراح) or Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

617
00:54:03,092 --> 00:54:08,255
give Bay’ah(بيعة) to one of them, either Umar(عُمَر) or Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة).

618
00:54:11,845 --> 00:54:18,485
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he jumped ahead and he grabbed the hand of Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) and said:

619
00:54:18,609 --> 00:54:20,516
"I give you the Bay’ah(بيعة)"

620
00:54:22,436 --> 00:54:24,070
that’s it, he put him on the spot.

621
00:54:25,127 --> 00:54:26,287
You cannot back out of it.

622
00:54:27,332 --> 00:54:32,136
The narrator said, and then they just jumped on Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) giving him Bay’ah(بيعة)

623
00:54:32,511 --> 00:54:35,039
and they were about to step over Sa’ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عباده),

624
00:54:35,086 --> 00:54:38,342
because Sa’ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عباده) had a fever and he was sick.

625
00:54:38,603 --> 00:54:41,192
So, they were about to step over him, and crush him,

626
00:54:41,995 --> 00:54:46,827
that was how emotional they were and how bad they wanted to give Bay’ah(بيعة) to Abu Bakr(أبوبكر)

627
00:54:47,283 --> 00:54:52,501
So, this tells us Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in their disputes they were very honest and sincere.

628
00:54:53,626 --> 00:54:59,299
and when they would realize that their opinion was not the right opinion, they weren’t stubborn.

629
00:55:00,078 --> 00:55:03,230
These were the Ansaar(أنْصَار), who wanted to give Bay’ah(بيعة) to Sa’ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد ابن عباده)

630
00:55:03,483 --> 00:55:06,004
are now jumping ahead to give Bay’ah (بيعة) to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

631
00:55:06,350 --> 00:55:10,963
So, it wasn’t personal interest, it wasn’t jealousy, it wasn’t selfishness.

632
00:55:11,466 --> 00:55:14,837
They thought that they had the rightful claim to it,

633
00:55:15,130 --> 00:55:18,978
 and when they realized that it belongs to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), they gave him the Bay’ah(بيعة).

634
00:55:21,215 --> 00:55:25,219
Next day in the Masjid(مسجد), because this was a private Bay’ah(بيعة) given in a private meeting.

635
00:55:25,550 --> 00:55:29,981
Next day Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) walks in, Umar(عُمَر) goes and stands on the pulpit

636
00:55:30,164 --> 00:55:35,031
and he asks everyone in the Masjid(مسجد) to give a Bay’ah(بيعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

637
00:55:36,004 --> 00:55:38,901
Dear brothers and sisters! There is very important thing to learn here

638
00:55:39,425 --> 00:55:43,437
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was a man of initiative, he would take the initiative.

639
00:55:44,080 --> 00:55:47,709
There are sometimes things that you cannot do, it's not right to come from you.

640
00:55:48,049 --> 00:55:51,453
Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) cannot go around people and telling them give him Bay’ah(بيعة) and he didn't.

641
00:55:53,613 --> 00:55:56,038
Sometimes, we wait for our leaders to do everything.

642
00:55:56,432 --> 00:56:00,607
There are something that our leaders cannot do, either because they are incapable of doing it,

643
00:56:00,907 --> 00:56:02,437
either because they don’t want to do it,

644
00:56:03,080 --> 00:56:05,750
or it could be because it's not appropriate for them to do it.

645
00:56:06,932 --> 00:56:10,863
You need to have the initiative and go and do it.

646
00:56:11,993 --> 00:56:19,945
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) he did not call people to give him Khilafah(خِلَافَه), he called people to give it to Umar(عُمَر) or Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة)

647
00:56:20,243 --> 00:56:25,145
but Umar(عمر) knew that, it belongs to Abu Bakr(أبوبكر), so he took the initiative and he did it

648
00:56:26,182 --> 00:56:27,915
and then he did it in the Masjid(مسجد) again.

649
00:56:28,806 --> 00:56:33,931
There is a lot of passiveness among the Muslims today, we need to throw that behind and be proactive.

650
00:56:34,442 --> 00:56:41,355
Take the initiative, when there is something that is right and you are the one who could do it, go ahead and do it don’t wait.

651
00:56:42,466 --> 00:56:45,711
The leader was Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) but Umar(عُمَر) went ahead and did it

652
00:56:46,207 --> 00:56:49,972
because if he is gonna seek permission from Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) to do it, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) would refused.

653
00:56:52,801 --> 00:56:55,442
He went ahead and he put him on the spot and he gave him Bay’ah(بيعة).

654
00:56:55,903 --> 00:56:58,883
And then in the Masjid(مسجد), he was the one recruiting the Bay’ah(بيعة),

655
00:56:59,856 --> 00:57:01,548
soliciting the Bay’ah(بيعة) from the people.

656
00:57:04,394 --> 00:57:10,303
He was a man of initiative and we need that trait, attribute today, we need it badly.

657
00:57:14,907 --> 00:57:22,234
Some incidence that happened during the time of the khilafah(خلافة) of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه.

658
00:57:24,892 --> 00:57:34,214
There was a man called Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي), in Yemen, he claimed to be a prophet.

659
00:57:34,928 --> 00:57:36,689
This was a man in Yemen, who claimed to be a Prophet.

660
00:57:37,119 --> 00:57:40,386
During the last days of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

661
00:57:40,973 --> 00:57:45,395
Rasool Ullah saw a dream where he is wearing two bracelets of gold

662
00:57:47,407 --> 00:57:50,685
and then he looked at them and they flew away from his hand.

663
00:57:52,314 --> 00:57:57,537
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I interpret those to be liar of Yemen and liar of Yamamah(يمامه).

664
00:57:58,112 --> 00:58:01,178
There were two men, who claimed to be prophets in the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

665
00:58:01,252 --> 00:58:07,547
Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) in Yemen and Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه الكذاب) in Al-Yamamah(يمامه).

666
00:58:08,204 --> 00:58:11,764
They came in the form of gold, so gold doesn’t mean good things in dreams.

667
00:58:11,788 --> 00:58:13,646
Whenever you see gold that's not a good sign.

668
00:58:14,651 --> 00:58:23,096
In this dream it meant these two liars, it also means the things that are fake, unreal, deceptive,

669
00:58:23,509 --> 00:58:25,945
 these are all meanings of gold in dreams.

670
00:58:27,879 --> 00:58:30,796
So, Rasool Ullah blew them and they just flew away,

671
00:58:31,621 --> 00:58:34,437
so that means that their Fitnah(فِتْنَه) is gonna go away.

672
00:58:35,255 --> 00:58:41,755
Anyways Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) his Fitnah(فِتْنَه) carried on, passed the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

673
00:58:41,818 --> 00:58:46,578
and the same with Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه الكذاب) but then it is Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), who ended their Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

674
00:58:48,557 --> 00:58:54,428
Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) arrested a man in Yemen called Abdullah Ibn Thawb(عبدالله بن ثوب).

675
00:58:54,979 --> 00:58:58,224
This was a Wali(ولي) of Allah a pious man.

676
00:58:59,064 --> 00:59:01,915
His Kuniyah(كنية) was Abu Muslim Al-Khawlaani(ابو مسلم الخولانى).

677
00:59:04,125 --> 00:59:08,660
Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) arrested him and he told him,

678
00:59:09,835 --> 00:59:14,388
Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?

679
00:59:15,721 --> 00:59:17,149
 He said, I cannot hear you,

680
00:59:18,930 --> 00:59:22,660
he said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah?

681
00:59:22,954 --> 00:59:23,970
He said: "Yes".

682
00:59:25,783 --> 00:59:28,662
So, to makes sure that, he doesn’t have hearing problems, so he asked him again,

683
00:59:30,596 --> 00:59:33,667
Do you bear witness that I am the messenger of Allah? He said: I cannot hear you.

684
00:59:34,706 --> 00:59:37,858
Do you bear witness that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah? He said: "Yes".

685
00:59:38,815 --> 00:59:41,742
So, Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) knew that he was playing games on him,

686
00:59:43,439 --> 00:59:45,774
so he ordered him to be burnt alive.

687
00:59:47,139 --> 00:59:50,188
They tied him up and they threw him in the fire,

688
00:59:53,108 --> 01:00:02,227
the only thing that burned on his body were the ropes that were tying his arms, he came out untouched,

689
01:00:03,246 --> 01:00:05,230
 he walked out of fire untouched.

690
01:00:06,712 --> 01:00:12,420
The deputies of Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود العنسي) said: "This man will be a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for us, drive him out of the land."

691
01:00:13,174 --> 01:00:19,164
 This is a Karamah(كرامة), send him out, so he was forced to leave Yemen and he went to Al-Madina.

692
01:00:20,652 --> 01:00:23,716
He enters Al-Masjid Nabawwi(مسجد النبوي) and this was during the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(أبوبكر)

693
01:00:24,081 --> 01:00:26,399
he goes into the Masjid Al-Nabawwi(مسجد النبوي) and prays

694
01:00:27,367 --> 01:00:29,159
and Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) was sitting with Umar(عمر)

695
01:00:30,877 --> 01:00:33,944
Umar(عُمَر) sees this foreign man, coming in, he never met him before.

696
01:00:35,787 --> 01:00:38,697
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب) walks up to him after he finishes, his Salah(صلاة) and he said:

697
01:00:41,694 --> 01:00:44,234
Are you from Yemen? He said: "Yes."

698
01:00:46,334 --> 01:00:51,211
He said: What happened that man, who was burnt in the fire and he came out free?

699
01:00:52,341 --> 01:00:54,964
He said: That man is Abdullah Ibn Thawb(عبدالله ابن ثوب),

700
01:00:56,332 --> 01:00:59,886
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب) said: I ask you in the Name of Allah, is it you?

701
01:01:01,161 --> 01:01:02,441
The man said, "Yes!".

702
01:01:04,369 --> 01:01:07,069
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب) embraced him and kissed him

703
01:01:08,167 --> 01:01:12,411
 and then he took him to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرألصديق) and he had him, sit between him and Abu Bakr(أبوبكر)

704
01:01:13,412 --> 01:01:18,422
and he said, praise be to Allah, who did not allow me to die,

705
01:01:18,968 --> 01:01:25,292
 until he made me see a man, who went through a miracles similar to the miracle of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

706
01:01:29,753 --> 01:01:33,186
First of all look at the Farasah(فراسه), the amazing Farasah(فراسه) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب)

707
01:01:33,690 --> 01:01:41,829
he sees this man, never meets him before and he knows that this is the man, who was burnt in the fire by just looking at his face.

708
01:01:42,472 --> 01:01:43,889
 An amazing Farasah(فراسه)

709
01:01:46,102 --> 01:01:49,388
and then the second thing, and this is blessing of Allah on this Ummah(امة),

710
01:01:50,015 --> 01:01:52,624
there are men in this Ummah(امة) who are not Prophets

711
01:01:53,986 --> 01:01:58,256
but they are friends of Allah(اولياء الله عزوجل) who went through Karamat(كرامات)

712
01:01:59,075 --> 01:02:01,948
that are similar to the miracles that were given to Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

713
01:02:03,598 --> 01:02:08,308
Abu Ala Al-Hadhrami(ابوالاعلى حضرمي) and we talked about him during our series on Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

714
01:02:08,723 --> 01:02:13,348
 he performed a miracle similar to the miracle of Musa عليه السّلام he walked on water.

715
01:02:15,097 --> 01:02:17,216
And here you have Abu Muslim Al-Khawlaani(أبومسلم ألخولاني)

716
01:02:17,645 --> 01:02:22,549
 he is burnt in the fire like Ibrahim عليه السّلام and he comes out unscathed, untouched.

717
01:02:25,764 --> 01:02:31,178
So, this is a blessed Ummah(امة), this is the greatest Ummah(امة) of all.

718
01:02:36,389 --> 01:02:41,605
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه had a reputation of being a very soft and compassionate man,

719
01:02:41,922 --> 01:02:45,550
so the Bedouins of Arabia, they want to take advantage of that,

720
01:02:45,574 --> 01:02:51,086
- you know these Bedouins are harsh and rough and they are attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

721
01:02:51,842 --> 01:02:55,087
and their profession was raiding caravans and oppressing others,

722
01:02:55,325 --> 01:02:57,771
so they felt that this is a soft man, we will take advantage of him.

723
01:02:59,396 --> 01:03:02,609
The name Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), means the father of the young lively camel,

724
01:03:02,633 --> 01:03:06,496
Bakr(بكر) is a young lively camel, it's not his real name, his real name is Abdullah(عبدالله)

725
01:03:08,186 --> 01:03:09,660
but this was his Kuniyah(كنيه).

726
01:03:10,516 --> 01:03:16,019
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)! Which is the father of the lively camel or the one of the lively camel.

727
01:03:16,539 --> 01:03:20,665
So, these tribes, they use to make fun of Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) and they would say; "Abul-faseel(أبوالفصيل)"

728
01:03:21,116 --> 01:03:24,943
the father of the infant camel, to mean that he is weak.

729
01:03:26,018 --> 01:03:30,701
Odaee Ubn Haatim(عديئ بن حاتم) was telling them, a day will come when you will realize that he was Abul Fahl Al-Akbar(ابوالفهل الاكبر),

730
01:03:31,049 --> 01:03:36,142
that he is the father of a great stallion, you will come to know that, be careful.

731
01:03:37,732 --> 01:03:40,747
Anyway one of these tribes decided that they don’t want to pay the Zakah(زكواة)

732
01:03:41,138 --> 01:03:42,171
we are not going to pay to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

733
01:03:42,211 --> 01:03:45,123
 we use to pay it to Rasool Allah ﷺ, we are not going to pay it, to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

734
01:03:46,467 --> 01:03:51,435
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) sends one army after another, one army after another and they came to realize that he is serious

735
01:03:51,729 --> 01:03:55,596
and he is not going to leave them alone, and they were losing big time.

736
01:03:56,477 --> 01:04:01,357
They eventually have to submit they came to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and what did they wanted to do?

737
01:04:01,730 --> 01:04:03,502
 They want to make a peace agreement.

738
01:04:04,622 --> 01:04:07,540
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) said: I am going to give you two choices:

739
01:04:08,590 --> 01:04:14,360
إَمَّا حَرْبٌ مُجَلِّيَّةْ اَوْ خُطَّةْ مُخْزِيَّةْ

740
01:04:14,922 --> 01:04:18,418
I give you two options, one a war of extermination

741
01:04:19,766 --> 01:04:25,058
the second a humiliating plan or peace agreement.

742
01:04:26,188 --> 01:04:28,895
They said: Well, we understand what, war of extermination means,

743
01:04:29,009 --> 01:04:31,434
you are going to wipe us out, that's one option.

744
01:04:31,527 --> 01:04:33,527
The second option, what do you mean by

745
01:04:33,553 --> 01:04:34,381
"خُطَّةْ مُخْزِيَّةْ ؟"

746
01:04:34,705 --> 01:04:37,154
A humiliating agreement? He said:

747
01:04:38,033 --> 01:04:44,611
"I want you to hand over all of your arms and then you follow the tails of your camels."

748
01:04:45,919 --> 01:04:49,082
To them, even among the people of Jahiliyah(جاهليه) in those days,

749
01:04:49,442 --> 01:04:54,421
a man without his arms is no different than his animals.

750
01:04:55,331 --> 01:04:59,726
If you don’t have weapons you are equal to a camel or a donkey or a horse.

751
01:05:00,425 --> 01:05:02,329
That was their perception in those days.

752
01:05:03,621 --> 01:05:07,872
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is telling them you hand over all your arms and you follow the tails of your camels.

753
01:05:08,118 --> 01:05:09,475
 You and your camels become equal.

754
01:05:11,482 --> 01:05:16,141
Number two: The spoils of wars, that we took from you, we weren't going to hand them back

755
01:05:16,349 --> 01:05:19,149
and anything that you took from us, you hand it over back to us.

756
01:05:20,176 --> 01:05:26,460
Number three: You publically testify that, the one you killed among us are going to Jannah(جنة)

757
01:05:26,816 --> 01:05:29,335
and the we killed among you are going to Hell fire.

758
01:05:30,113 --> 01:05:35,637
This is very humiliating thing for them to go around telling the people that the ones who died among us go to Hell fire

759
01:05:35,877 --> 01:05:37,788
and the ones whom we kill among them go to Jannah(جنة).

760
01:05:39,057 --> 01:05:46,047
And then he said: I want you to pay the blood money for the ones you killed among us

761
01:05:46,527 --> 01:05:49,615
and we don’t pay you anything for the ones whom we killed among you.

762
01:05:51,156 --> 01:05:56,536
And then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said, I want your advice, he is asking Umar(عُمَر).

763
01:05:57,417 --> 01:05:58,703
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said:

764
01:06:00,219 --> 01:06:06,405
Giving them a choice of war of extermination or a humiliating agreement I agree with that.

765
01:06:07,585 --> 01:06:13,711
Saying that they have to publically declare dead among them go to Hell fire and dead among us go to Jannah(جنة), I agree with that,

766
01:06:15,036 --> 01:06:19,880
 they pay us what they took from us and we don’t pay them back I agree with that.

767
01:06:21,033 --> 01:06:25,162
That they give up their weapons and that they follow their camels, I agree with that.

768
01:06:26,115 --> 01:06:31,789
But when you say that we don’t have to pay them blood money and they have to pay us blood money.

769
01:06:32,555 --> 01:06:35,301
The dead among us were Shuhada Fi Sabeelillah(شهداء فى سبيل الله)

770
01:06:35,341 --> 01:06:38,972
and their reward is on Allahعَزّ وجَلّ, so we don’t want any money from them.

771
01:06:39,556 --> 01:06:42,174
These are Shuhada(شهداء), they don’t pay anything for that.

772
01:06:42,262 --> 01:06:44,413
 It's an honor for them, that they died Fi Sabeelillah(في سبيل الله).

773
01:06:46,138 --> 01:06:50,915
So, he agreed with everything except with this clause in the agreement.

774
01:06:51,714 --> 01:06:55,203
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) gave these Murtadeen(مرتدين) a very different impression.

775
01:06:56,266 --> 01:06:58,817
He was very strict, when he needed to be,

776
01:06:58,885 --> 01:07:03,774
because this was Al-Haq(الحق) this was the truth, this was Fi Sabeelillah(في سبيل الله).

777
01:07:08,567 --> 01:07:10,041
Another incident that happened:

778
01:07:14,519 --> 01:07:20,749
There are two men, from the Araab(اعراب) the leaders of the Bedouin clans.

779
01:07:21,132 --> 01:07:24,504
Al-Aqra’a Bin Habis(الاقراع بن حابس) and Oayyena Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن)

780
01:07:25,145 --> 01:07:27,166
these two men were trouble makers

781
01:07:27,734 --> 01:07:30,488
they used to cause a lot of trouble in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

782
01:07:30,829 --> 01:07:32,781
and they were oscillate in and out of Islam.

783
01:07:33,593 --> 01:07:37,128
When they see the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is on the side of Rasool Ullah, they would go with him

784
01:07:37,394 --> 01:07:40,561
and whenever scale tilts to the Mushrikeen(مشركين) they would go with them.

785
01:07:41,475 --> 01:07:42,486
They were the people of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

786
01:07:43,827 --> 01:07:50,515
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to win them over because they were prominent people in their tribes.

787
01:07:51,170 --> 01:07:53,314
So, he was giving them from the Zakkah(زكواة)

788
01:07:53,512 --> 01:07:56,304
and he was giving them from the Ghanaim(غنائم) in order to win them over.

789
01:07:57,746 --> 01:08:03,775
And that is allowed in Daw'ah(دعوة) you can win over people by encouraging them by encouraging them, even if money is involved.

790
01:08:04,211 --> 01:08:08,414
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving them to soften their hearts to get a commitment from them,

791
01:08:08,604 --> 01:08:14,479
because he knows behind them are many people, who would become Muslim if, they become Muslim.

792
01:08:16,651 --> 01:08:20,484
These two men came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) when he was a Khalifah(خليفه) and they said;

793
01:08:20,565 --> 01:08:23,692
There is a waste land, it doesn’t belong to anyone,

794
01:08:24,874 --> 01:08:31,665
can you please give it to us, so that we will use it as a place of pasture for our cattle.

795
01:08:33,432 --> 01:08:40,447
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) didn’t see a problem with that, this land is a waste land, it doesn’t belong to anybody, so why not.

796
01:08:42,039 --> 01:08:45,785
He sort, he made a Shurah(شورى) with the Sahabah(صحابه), who were with him.

797
01:08:46,382 --> 01:08:48,783
He consulted them, they didn’t see a problem with that.

798
01:08:50,152 --> 01:08:55,561
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق), he writes a document,

799
01:08:56,755 --> 01:09:02,302
that this piece of land, we say in America " A Title", titled that this belongs to you,

800
01:09:03,435 --> 01:09:05,905
he wrote down that, this land belongs to them

801
01:09:05,929 --> 01:09:09,017
- and he writes down that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is one of the witnesses.

802
01:09:09,056 --> 01:09:10,422
Now Umar(عمر) wasn’t present.

803
01:09:11,030 --> 01:09:17,767
So, he has a name of Umar(عُمَر) and he gives this document to Al-Aqra’a(اقراع) and ‘Oyyaynah(عيينة),

804
01:09:17,834 --> 01:09:23,914
so they go to find Umar(عمر) so that he can sign on it, because his name is there, so he has to sign on it.

805
01:09:24,786 --> 01:09:26,432
He is one of the Shoohud(شهود) he is the witness.

806
01:09:27,551 --> 01:09:34,972
So, to Aqra’a Bin Habis(الاقراع بن حابس) and Oyyaynah(عيينة) they go and they find Umar Ibn Al-Khattab applying Tor, Qatraan(قطران) to his camel.

807
01:09:35,332 --> 01:09:40,453
They use to apply Tor, it's oil whatever it is , it's called in Arabic Qatraan(قطران).

808
01:09:41,620 --> 01:09:46,240
They use to apply to their camels to cure them from the flees.

809
01:09:47,121 --> 01:09:52,232
So, they would apply this Tor, he was applying this Tor to his camel, working hard on his camel.

810
01:09:52,764 --> 01:09:58,299
Now, the Sahabah(صحابه) would do this type of work that you may be assume that a servant should be doing it,

811
01:09:58,769 --> 01:10:00,559
 but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن خطاب) was doing it himself.

812
01:10:01,863 --> 01:10:05,103
So Al-Aqra’a(الاقراع) and Oyyaynah(عيينه) these are rough men, they are from the desert.

813
01:10:05,788 --> 01:10:07,541
They come to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and they say

814
01:10:08,969 --> 01:10:11,937
We have this document from Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) the Khalifah(خليفه),

815
01:10:12,260 --> 01:10:14,591
and it has your name on it and we want you to sign it.

816
01:10:14,884 --> 01:10:16,781
So, shall we read or you read?

817
01:10:17,810 --> 01:10:19,360
He said: Well you see, that I am busy,

818
01:10:20,222 --> 01:10:24,735
so if you want to read so go ahead and if you want me to read it then you will have to wait until I finish.

819
01:10:25,710 --> 01:10:27,536
They said: Alright we will go ahead and read it.

820
01:10:27,959 --> 01:10:31,029
So, they read it, what does Umar(عُمَر) do?

821
01:10:32,387 --> 01:10:37,346
He stands up, he grabs the document and he spits on it and he wipes everything in there.

822
01:10:38,218 --> 01:10:39,791
That’s it the title is gone.

823
01:10:40,749 --> 01:10:46,228
Al-Aqra’a(الاقراع) and Oyyaynah(عيينة) were angry, they were exploding and they were arguing with Umar(عُمَر).

824
01:10:46,844 --> 01:10:48,244
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told them,

825
01:10:48,434 --> 01:10:55,421
Rasool Allah ﷺ use to give you when Islam was weak, today Islam is strong, so go and work for yourselves.

826
01:10:57,259 --> 01:10:58,017
Go and work!

827
01:10:58,111 --> 01:11:03,561
You are not going to get anything for free Rasool Ullah used to give you, yesterday because Islam was weak we don’t need you now.

828
01:11:06,253 --> 01:11:11,856
They were fuming they went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) they were just steamed, coming out of their heads.

829
01:11:13,647 --> 01:11:17,904
They said: "We do not know who is the Khalifah(خليفه) you or Umar(عُمَر)?"

830
01:11:20,001 --> 01:11:21,876
Who is making the decision here?

831
01:11:22,990 --> 01:11:24,108
What did Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) say?

832
01:11:24,522 --> 01:11:29,526
Abu Bakr said: He is the Khalifah(خليفه) if he wants.

833
01:11:30,116 --> 01:11:37,824
Now you know when you are in a position of administration and somebody steps into your territory, you become very, very sensitive.

834
01:11:39,021 --> 01:11:42,454
The turf wars they cause so much hatred in the hearts.

835
01:11:42,993 --> 01:11:44,175
You are stepping over my toes.

836
01:11:44,398 --> 01:11:49,901
You are getting into my realm of sphere of influence whatever, and fight starts

837
01:11:51,594 --> 01:11:55,475
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: If he wants to become a Khalifah(خليفه) he can be the Khalifah(خليفه).

838
01:11:56,688 --> 01:12:01,614
They were doing it for the sake of Allah, they were not doing it for their personal interests.

839
01:12:01,638 --> 01:12:05,952
Even though the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is the greatest status that exists on the face of the earth.

840
01:12:06,460 --> 01:12:14,736
There is no status at all higher than the Khalifah(خليفه) in the Muslim or non Muslim world, Khalifah(خليفه) is the highest.

841
01:12:15,334 --> 01:12:16,763
their is nothing above you but Allah.

842
01:12:18,617 --> 01:12:26,706
Nevertheless, they were so easy with it, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) didn’t have problem of giving it to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

843
01:12:27,686 --> 01:12:31,944
so you should be wondering today how come Muslims are fighting?

844
01:12:33,317 --> 01:12:35,681
We have nothing, we have no Khilafah(خِلَافَه), we have no wealth,

845
01:12:35,705 --> 01:12:38,651
we have nothing, and we are still fighting on these small territories.

846
01:12:39,769 --> 01:12:42,373
It's foolish it doesn’t make any sense whatsoever.

847
01:12:42,851 --> 01:12:47,326
I mean you fight on Khilafah(خِلَافَه) they didn’t fight in the times of Sahabah(صحابه) but then later on

848
01:12:47,463 --> 01:12:51,030
later on in times of Bannu Ummayah(بنو اميه) and Bannu Abbas(بنو عباس) they were fighting on Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

849
01:12:51,486 --> 01:12:55,457
It's wrong but at least there is a reason for them to fight.

850
01:12:55,481 --> 01:12:58,278
You know, that they are fighting on something big even though it's wrong.

851
01:12:58,563 --> 01:13:02,831
But now what are Muslims fighting on? NOTHING!! It's miserable.

852
01:13:06,007 --> 01:13:08,514
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said, if he wants to become a Khalifah(خليفه), he can become a Khalifah(خليفه),

853
01:13:08,656 --> 01:13:10,082
Umar(عُمَر) comes in and he was angry.

854
01:13:10,745 --> 01:13:14,442
He comes to the Khalifah(خليفه) and look at how he speaks to the Khalifah(خليفه),

855
01:13:15,313 --> 01:13:19,392
he said: "This land, does it belongs to you, or it belongs to Muslims?"

856
01:13:20,743 --> 01:13:23,632
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه said: "It belongs to the Muslims."

857
01:13:24,991 --> 01:13:27,133
He said: "Then how come you giveit, to these two men?"

858
01:13:27,827 --> 01:13:31,694
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) said: "I have made a Shura(شورى), I've consulted these Sahabah(صحابه)".

859
01:13:32,884 --> 01:13:33,999
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said:

860
01:13:34,187 --> 01:13:37,868
You have consulted these Sahabah(صحابه) but did you consult all of the Muslims?

861
01:13:39,176 --> 01:13:43,916
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: "O Umar(عُمَر) I have already told you before,

862
01:13:44,543 --> 01:13:49,192
 that you are more competent to do this job then me but you refused.

863
01:13:51,722 --> 01:13:54,674
I've already told you Umar(عُمَر) I wanted you to become a Khalifah(خليفه)

864
01:13:55,004 --> 01:13:59,406
you are stronger than me you are more competent then me, but you are the one, who refused.

865
01:14:00,723 --> 01:14:02,793
Can you imagine a leader today saying that?

866
01:14:04,354 --> 01:14:11,999
Can you imagine a president or a king or a prime minister saying that publically that you ought to be the leader you are better than me,

867
01:14:12,759 --> 01:14:18,112
in the greatest democracy of the democracies you wouldn't find that let alone in tyranny of the Islamic world.

868
01:14:21,055 --> 01:14:23,656
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that was the way of Sahabah(صحابه).

869
01:14:23,680 --> 01:14:24,990
 "وَكَانُوْا أَقَلِّ النَّاسِ تَكَلُّفَا"

870
01:14:25,015 --> 01:14:26,358
They were the least superficial.

871
01:14:26,897 --> 01:14:29,612
They were very simple, easy, straight forward and honest people.

872
01:14:30,896 --> 01:14:33,733
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is saying it, publically in front of the people.

873
01:14:33,982 --> 01:14:36,235
In front of Al-Aqra’a Bin Habis(الاقراع بن حابس) and Oayyena Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن).

874
01:14:36,497 --> 01:14:38,318
I wanted you to become a Khalifah(خليفه) but you refused.

875
01:14:41,026 --> 01:14:43,876
But these were men who were living for the Akhirah(آخرة), they were not living for the Duniyah(دنيا)

876
01:14:44,582 --> 01:14:49,297
Their minds were connected to Akhirah(آخرة), their eyes were fixed on Jannah(جنة),

877
01:14:50,106 --> 01:14:53,700
Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) to them was just a bridge, Aabiris Sabeel(عابر سبيل الله) a traveler.

878
01:14:59,588 --> 01:15:03,664
Finally, Jama’al Qur’an(جمع القرءآن):

879
01:15:07,979 --> 01:15:15,531
During the Khilfah(خِلَافه) of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) in the Haroob(حروب) of Ar-Riddah(الرداء)

880
01:15:17,095 --> 01:15:21,113
 specifically in the wars of Yamamah(يمامه) against Musailmah Al-Kadhab(مسيلمه الكذاب)

881
01:15:21,923 --> 01:15:28,989
hundreds of Sahabah(صحابه) were killed and many of them were Hufaaz(حفاظ) of Qur’an, memorizers of Qur’an,

882
01:15:31,061 --> 01:15:32,599
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) goes to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and says;

883
01:15:32,723 --> 01:15:34,223
 "لَقَدْ إِسْتَحَّرَّ الْقَتْل"

884
01:15:37,319 --> 01:15:43,828
The death is going through the memorizers of the Qur’an

885
01:15:46,429 --> 01:15:50,845
 and I am afraid that death will take them away in one battle, after another battle,

886
01:15:51,756 --> 01:15:53,330
so you have to compile Qur’an.

887
01:15:54,752 --> 01:15:58,684
Up to that stage Qur’an was not compiled in one book.

888
01:15:59,427 --> 01:16:09,107
Qur’an, if you want a Mus'haf(مصحف) it would be a huge sack of bones, pieces of wood, leaves and leather.

889
01:16:10,223 --> 01:16:13,484
They use to write it on the shoulder bone of camel which is big, plate.

890
01:16:14,012 --> 01:16:17,269
They would write it on a piece of wood, they would write it on leather,

891
01:16:17,901 --> 01:16:20,139
they would write it on palm leaves.

892
01:16:20,925 --> 01:16:23,833
So, the Mus'haf(مصحف) would be a huge sack,

893
01:16:24,509 --> 01:16:27,603
and it wasn't really compiled in one place and was spread around.

894
01:16:28,392 --> 01:16:30,182
Every Sahabi(صحابي) would have a one piece of it.

895
01:16:30,719 --> 01:16:37,340
Umar(عُمَر) said: If the ones, who memorize Qur’an are dead Mus'haf(مصحف) would be lost.

896
01:16:37,430 --> 01:16:39,258
So, you have to compile it together.

897
01:16:40,221 --> 01:16:43,964
Abu Bakr Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: " How you want me to do something that Rasool Allah ﷺ did not do?"

898
01:16:46,992 --> 01:16:47,928
"إِنَّمَا اَنَا مُتَّبِعْ

899
01:16:48,052 --> 01:16:50,252
" I am a follower, I am not an innovator.

900
01:16:50,874 --> 01:16:56,612
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) kept on, arguing with Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) again and again, until he convinced him.

901
01:16:57,213 --> 01:17:02,074
That, this is the Mas'laha(مصلحة) that this is a good thing to do and it's not an innovation.

902
01:17:03,241 --> 01:17:09,218
 Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) agreed, and then they decided to appoint that task Zaid bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت),

903
01:17:09,737 --> 01:17:12,835
one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), young man in his twenties,

904
01:17:13,893 --> 01:17:21,033
imagine this duty this huge project is handed over to Zaid bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت).

905
01:17:23,345 --> 01:17:29,934
So, Zaid رضي الله عنه was summoned to come and meet the Khalifah(خليفه)

906
01:17:30,729 --> 01:17:32,385
Umar(عُمَر) was sitting next to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

907
01:17:33,508 --> 01:17:36,749
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: "Umar(عُمَر) came to me and said, that

908
01:17:37,468 --> 01:17:43,589
death is taking away the lives of many of the memorizers of Qur’an

909
01:17:46,875 --> 01:17:50,963
and we want you to be the one, who compiles Al-Mus'haf(المصحف)

910
01:17:51,719 --> 01:17:55,267
Zaid(زيد) said: "How do you want me to do something, that Rasool Allah ﷺ did not do?

911
01:17:56,475 --> 01:18:02,745
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said, well that’s what I said, but then Umar(عُمَر) convinced me, and they convinced Zaid(زيد).

912
01:18:03,531 --> 01:18:08,525
Zaid(زيد) said: If they would have told me move a mountain from its place

913
01:18:09,114 --> 01:18:14,363
it would have been an easier task then the task they have gave me.

914
01:18:15,527 --> 01:18:22,910
He felt that it was so heavy of a task, so greater responsibility, it would be easier for him to move a mountain from its place.

915
01:18:24,620 --> 01:18:27,026
However, he did it, and he did it perfectly

916
01:18:27,673 --> 01:18:33,924
and he combined the Al-Mus'haf(المصحف) in one original copy that was left with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

917
01:18:34,786 --> 01:18:37,203
And that was the first compilation of Qur’an

918
01:18:37,544 --> 01:18:40,212
 and then Uthman(عثمان) made copies of that original copy.

919
01:18:41,833 --> 01:18:47,690
So, Uthman(عثمان) made copies of original copy that was made by Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

920
01:18:51,488 --> 01:18:55,861
One comment to make one this: Where were the Hufaaz(حفاظ) of Al-Qur’an?

921
01:18:56,309 --> 01:19:00,276
Where were the memorizers of Qur’an, How come they were dying, Where were they?

922
01:19:01,455 --> 01:19:02,467
THEY WERE IN THE LINE OF FIRE.!

923
01:19:04,448 --> 01:19:08,869
The memorizers of the Qur’an were not hiding away in their Masajid(مساجد)

924
01:19:10,470 --> 01:19:15,904
 pretending to be scholars, leading the Salah(صلاة) and staying away from trouble.

925
01:19:16,877 --> 01:19:20,066
The memorizers of the Qur’an in those days were in the line of fire.

926
01:19:20,845 --> 01:19:26,926
Salim Moula Abi Hudhayfah(سالم مولى ابى حذيفة), he was the one, given the banner of war

927
01:19:28,828 --> 01:19:31,297
 and they told him; "Are you up for that challenge?

928
01:19:32,383 --> 01:19:35,582
Are you sure that you are able to do this task?" He said:

929
01:19:35,681 --> 01:19:38,961
بِئْثَ حَامِلْ القُرْآنِ أَنَا إِنْ أُوْتِيْتُمْ مِنْ قِبَلِيْ

930
01:19:39,360 --> 01:19:43,505
I am the worse carrier of Qur’an if you are attacked from my side.

931
01:19:44,720 --> 01:19:49,181
How can I be a carrier of Qur’an if I allow you to be attacked from my side?

932
01:19:50,690 --> 01:19:52,482
That was the understanding that they had.

933
01:19:52,948 --> 01:19:56,322
If you are somebody, who memorize the Qur’an, you need to be on the front line.

934
01:19:56,946 --> 01:19:59,770
You need to be, the one practicing the Qur’an.

935
01:20:00,274 --> 01:20:01,306
But Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

936
01:20:01,346 --> 01:20:05,637
"The time will come when people will memorize the Qur’an and it doesn’t go beyond their throats.

937
01:20:06,047 --> 01:20:08,867
All what they can do, is to recite it they don’t know what it means?

938
01:20:09,062 --> 01:20:14,873
And they are not practicing what it says and these are very dangerous people.

939
01:20:15,467 --> 01:20:17,100
And Rasool Allah ﷺ warned us from them.

940
01:20:17,870 --> 01:20:20,212
Qur’an can be an evidence for you or against you.

941
01:20:20,495 --> 01:20:24,238
If you know it and don’t apply it that person ends up going into Hell fire.

942
01:20:25,229 --> 01:20:28,233
So, the Huffaaz(حفاظ) of Qur’an in those days were on the front line.

943
01:20:29,338 --> 01:20:32,057
And that’s why they were Huffaaz(حفاظ) of Qur’an.

944
01:20:32,798 --> 01:20:35,261
Haafiz(حافظ) of Qur’an means somebody, who is protecting Qur’an,

945
01:20:35,525 --> 01:20:39,812
and you protect Qur’an by living it and by promoting it and that what they were doing.

946
01:20:41,365 --> 01:20:46,298
This was the life of Umar(عُمَر) with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

947
01:20:46,717 --> 01:20:50,154
In Sha Allah(ان شاء الله) from tomorrow, we will start with the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar(عُمَر).

948
01:20:51,096 --> 01:20:55,316
We might have to do double session on some of those evenings

949
01:20:55,340 --> 01:21:00,078
because we might be running a bit late, we're bit behind schedule.

950
01:21:00,742 --> 01:21:04,392
So, I hope you are alright doing a double session

951
01:21:04,821 --> 01:21:09,061
on some of those evenings maybe tomorrow night we'll have another session 45 minutes each,

952
01:21:09,421 --> 01:21:11,864
 with a break in between, we'll how it goes In Sha Allah(إن شاء الله) anyway.

953
01:21:12,327 --> 01:21:16,109
We don’t have time for questions tonight. So

954
01:21:16,134 --> 01:21:18,746
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

955
01:21:19,011 --> 01:21:22,939
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

956
01:21:23,217 --> 01:21:27,467
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

957
01:21:27,499 --> 01:21:30,949
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

958
01:21:31,796 --> 01:21:36,005
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE.

